 %}";}}i:2;a:1:{s:7:"message";s:46:"Thank you for sharing your experience with us.";}i:3;a:1:{s:5:"reset";b:1;}}}}}s:34:"0e25d4667c6ea0efec58009988cb2668sc";a:5:{s:5:"title";s:14:"Privacy Policy";s:7:"summary";s:44:"How GODC collects and uses your information.";s:8:"metadata";a:1:{s:11:"description";s:118:"Read the GODC privacy policy: what information we collect through our website and forms and how we use and protect it.";}s:4:"hero";a:2:{s:7:"eyebrow";s:5:"Legal";s:5:"title";s:14:"Privacy Policy";}s:3:"cta";a:4:{s:5:"title";s:29:"Questions about your privacy?";s:4:"text";s:45:"Contact our team and we will be glad to help.";s:12:"button_label";s:10:"Contact Us";s:11:"button_link";s:20:"/book-a-consultation";}}s:34:"74633560f7b1b72c775b48e5d3d6dae7sc";a:9:{s:5:"title";s:12:"Our Services";s:7:"summary";s:118:"Specialist clinical nutrition and lifestyle medicine services for prevention, chronic disease management and recovery.";s:8:"metadata";a:2:{s:11:"description";s:184:"Explore GODC’s clinical and critical care nutrition services: obesity, diabetes, heart, kidney, neurological, musculoskeletal, geriatric, oncology and preventive nutrition in Lahore.";s:8:"keywords";s:133:"clinical nutrition services Lahore, lifestyle medicine, medical nutrition therapy, critical care nutrition, diabetes diet, renal diet";}s:4:"hero";a:5:{s:7:"eyebrow";s:12:"Our Services";s:5:"title";s:49:"Specialist surgical & clinical nutrition services";s:4:"text";s:249:"From bariatric, diabetes and advanced laparoscopic surgery to clinical and critical care nutrition and lifestyle medicine, our doctors and specialists deliver personalised, evidence-based care for medical conditions, recovery and long-term wellness.";s:12:"button_label";s:8:"Get Help";s:11:"button_link";s:20:"/book-a-consultation";}s:10:"categories";a:10:{i:0;a:4:{s:5:"title";s:34:"Clinical & Critical Care Nutrition";s:4:"text";s:98:"ICU, enteral and parenteral nutrition, post-surgical recovery and organ-failure nutrition support.";s:4:"link";s:41:"/our-services/clinical-critical-nutrition";s:10:"link_label";s:21:"View the full service";}i:1;a:4:{s:5:"title";s:26:"Obesity & Metabolic Health";s:4:"text";s:123:"Medically guided weight management and metabolic care for obesity, metabolic syndrome, insulin resistance and dyslipidemia.";s:4:"link";s:38:"/our-services/obesity-metabolic-health";s:10:"link_label";s:21:"View the full service";}i:2;a:4:{s:5:"title";s:25:"Cardiometabolic Disorders";s:4:"text";s:93:"Nutrition and lifestyle therapy for hypertension, type 1 and type 2 diabetes and prediabetes.";s:4:"link";s:39:"/our-services/cardiometabolic-disorders";s:10:"link_label";s:21:"View the full service";}i:3;a:4:{s:5:"title";s:23:"Cardiovascular Diseases";s:4:"text";s:109:"Heart-focused nutrition, rehabilitation and risk-factor management for coronary, stroke and vascular disease.";s:4:"link";s:37:"/our-services/cardiovascular-diseases";s:10:"link_label";s:21:"View the full service";}i:4;a:4:{s:5:"title";s:21:"Specialized Nutrition";s:4:"text";s:106:"Condition-specific nutrition for oncology, gastrointestinal, liver and stress-related digestive disorders.";s:4:"link";s:35:"/our-services/specialized-nutrition";s:10:"link_label";s:21:"View the full service";}i:5;a:4:{s:5:"title";s:37:"Geriatric & Palliative Care Nutrition";s:4:"text";s:78:"Compassionate nutrition for frailty, cachexia, dysphagia and end-of-life care.";s:4:"link";s:49:"/our-services/geriatric-palliative-care-nutrition";s:10:"link_label";s:21:"View the full service";}i:6;a:4:{s:5:"title";s:32:"Aesthetic & Preventive Nutrition";s:4:"text";s:81:"Preventive and aesthetic nutrition for weight, skin, hair and long-term wellness.";s:4:"link";s:44:"/our-services/aesthetic-preventive-nutrition";s:10:"link_label";s:21:"View the full service";}i:7;a:4:{s:5:"title";s:22:"Neurological Disorders";s:4:"text";s:101:"Brain-supportive nutrition for stroke rehabilitation, dementia, Parkinson’s disease and neuropathy.";s:4:"link";s:36:"/our-services/neurological-disorders";s:10:"link_label";s:21:"View the full service";}i:8;a:4:{s:5:"title";s:15:"Renal Disorders";s:4:"text";s:74:"Kidney-safe nutrition for chronic kidney disease and diabetic nephropathy.";s:4:"link";s:29:"/our-services/renal-disorders";s:10:"link_label";s:21:"View the full service";}i:9;a:4:{s:5:"title";s:25:"Musculoskeletal Disorders";s:4:"text";s:93:"Nutrition to protect bone, joint and muscle health in arthritis, sarcopenia and osteoporosis.";s:4:"link";s:39:"/our-services/musculoskeletal-disorders";s:10:"link_label";s:21:"View the full service";}}s:13:"service_items";a:47:{i:0;a:4:{s:8:"category";s:34:"Clinical & Critical Care Nutrition";s:5:"title";s:36:"ICU NUTRITION (ENTERAL / PARENTERAL)";s:4:"text";s:214:"Critically ill patients need precise nutritional support at every stage of intensive care. We design and monitor enteral and parenteral feeding plans that protect lean mass, support organ function and aid recovery.";s:3:"why";s:120:"Our critical care team calculates, delivers and adjusts feeding daily alongside your treating consultants and ICU staff.";}i:1;a:4:{s:8:"category";s:34:"Clinical & Critical Care Nutrition";s:5:"title";s:25:"Sepsis & Trauma Nutrition";s:4:"text";s:211:"Sepsis and major trauma trigger rapid muscle breakdown and heavy metabolic demand. We provide protein and energy focused feeding strategies that stabilise metabolism, reduce complications during the acute phase.";s:3:"why";s:119:"We match nutrition delivery to each phase of illness, from resuscitation through to active rehabilitation and recovery.";}i:2;a:4:{s:8:"category";s:34:"Clinical & Critical Care Nutrition";s:5:"title";s:23:"Post-Surgical Nutrition";s:4:"text";s:219:"Recovery after surgery depends heavily on adequate protein, energy and micronutrient intake. We prepare pre and post operative nutrition plans that support wound healing, reduce infection risk and shorten hospital stay.";s:3:"why";s:107:"We work directly with surgical teams to plan feeding before admission and continue support after discharge.";}i:3;a:4:{s:8:"category";s:34:"Clinical & Critical Care Nutrition";s:5:"title";s:31:"Organ Failure Nutrition Support";s:4:"text";s:234:"Liver, kidney, cardiac and respiratory failure each demand carefully adjusted nutrition. We build individualised plans that balance protein, fluid, sodium and electrolytes while meeting energy needs without overloading failing organs.";s:3:"why";s:107:"Our plans are reviewed against live laboratory results so nutrition remains safe as organ function changes.";}i:4;a:4:{s:8:"category";s:34:"Clinical & Critical Care Nutrition";s:5:"title";s:32:"TPN (Total Parenteral Nutrition)";s:4:"text";s:213:"When the gut cannot be used safely, intravenous nutrition becomes essential. We formulate, deliver and monitor total parenteral nutrition with close attention to line safety, and timely transition to oral feeding.";s:3:"why";s:123:"Every TPN prescription is compounded, monitored and adjusted daily under close specialist medical and pharmacy supervision.";}i:5;a:4:{s:8:"category";s:26:"Obesity & Metabolic Health";s:5:"title";s:7:"Obesity";s:4:"text";s:222:"Obesity is a complex medical condition influenced by hormones, behaviour, environment and genetics. We provide structured, medically supervised weight management combining nutrition therapy and ongoing clinical monitoring.";s:3:"why";s:100:"We treat obesity as a medical condition, not a willpower problem, with evidence based clinical care.";}i:6;a:4:{s:8:"category";s:26:"Obesity & Metabolic Health";s:5:"title";s:18:"Metabolic Syndrome";s:4:"text";s:233:"Raised blood pressure, blood sugar, waist circumference and abnormal lipids often occur together. We address these linked risk factors with one coordinated plan that improves metabolic health and lowers long term cardiovascular risk.";s:3:"why";s:112:"One integrated plan targets every component of the syndrome instead of treating each abnormal result separately.";}i:7;a:4:{s:8:"category";s:26:"Obesity & Metabolic Health";s:5:"title";s:18:"Insulin Resistance";s:4:"text";s:214:"Insulin resistance often develops silently years before diabetes appears. We use targeted assessment, dietary restructuring, activity prescription and sleep and stress support to protect long term metabolic health.";s:3:"why";s:110:"Early detection allows us to reverse insulin resistance before it progresses into established type 2 diabetes.";}i:8;a:4:{s:8:"category";s:26:"Obesity & Metabolic Health";s:5:"title";s:12:"Dyslipidemia";s:4:"text";s:224:"Abnormal cholesterol and triglyceride levels are a major driver of cardiovascular disease. We combine dietary fat quality, weight management and lifestyle change with medical review to bring your lipid profile within target.";s:3:"why";s:124:"Nutrition therapy works alongside your prescribed medication to improve lipid results and overall cardiovascular protection.";}i:9;a:4:{s:8:"category";s:26:"Obesity & Metabolic Health";s:5:"title";s:27:"NAFLD / Fatty Liver Disease";s:4:"text";s:218:"Fatty liver disease is common, often silent and largely reversible in its early stages. We deliver structured nutrition, gradual weight reduction and lifestyle change to lower liver fat, inflammation and fibrosis risk.";s:3:"why";s:103:"We track liver enzymes and body composition together to confirm real, measurable improvement over time.";}i:10;a:4:{s:8:"category";s:25:"Cardiometabolic Disorders";s:5:"title";s:12:"Hypertension";s:4:"text";s:224:"High blood pressure rarely causes symptoms but quietly damages the heart, brain and kidneys. We deliver sodium, potassium, weight and stress focused therapy alongside medical care to achieve sustained blood pressure control.";s:3:"why";s:108:"Our lifestyle programmes are designed to support, not replace, the medication your physician has prescribed.";}i:11;a:4:{s:8:"category";s:25:"Cardiometabolic Disorders";s:5:"title";s:24:"Type 1 Diabetes Mellitus";s:4:"text";s:208:"Living with type 1 diabetes requires precise, flexible daily decisions around food and insulin. We provide carbohydrate counting, activity planning that improve glucose stability without limiting normal life.";s:3:"why";s:101:"We teach practical skills that let you adjust confidently around meals, exercise, travel and illness.";}i:12;a:4:{s:8:"category";s:25:"Cardiometabolic Disorders";s:5:"title";s:24:"Type 2 Diabetes Mellitus";s:4:"text";s:220:"Type 2 diabetes can often be improved, and sometimes reversed, with intensive lifestyle therapy. We combine structured nutrition, physical activity, weight reduction and glucose monitoring to achieve fewer complications.";s:3:"why";s:120:"Our remission focused programmes are medically supervised, with safe, planned adjustment of glucose lowering medication.";}i:13;a:4:{s:8:"category";s:25:"Cardiometabolic Disorders";s:5:"title";s:11:"Prediabetes";s:4:"text";s:228:"Prediabetes is a clear warning sign and a valuable opportunity to change direction. We provide early, structured intervention that restores normal glucose levels and significantly reduces your risk of developing type 2 diabetes.";s:3:"why";s:91:"Acting at this stage is the most effective and least invasive point to protect your health.";}i:14;a:4:{s:8:"category";s:23:"Cardiovascular Diseases";s:5:"title";s:29:"Coronary Artery Disease (CAD)";s:4:"text";s:230:"Narrowed coronary arteries restrict blood flow to the heart muscle and increase cardiac risk. We provide heart focused nutrition, activity and risk factor management that supports arterial health and reduces future cardiac events.";s:3:"why";s:109:"Our cardiac nutrition plans follow current international guidelines and are tailored to your medical history.";}i:15;a:4:{s:8:"category";s:23:"Cardiovascular Diseases";s:5:"title";s:14:"Rehabilitation";s:4:"text";s:220:"Recovery after a cardiac event, stent or bypass surgery needs structure, supervision and confidence. We deliver graded activity guidance, nutrition therapy and risk factor control to help you return safely to daily life.";s:3:"why";s:101:"Rehabilitation is paced to your capacity and reviewed regularly as your strength and stamina improve.";}i:16;a:4:{s:8:"category";s:23:"Cardiovascular Diseases";s:5:"title";s:12:"Stroke (CVA)";s:4:"text";s:228:"After a stroke, nutrition supports brain recovery, swallowing safety and prevention of further events. We provide texture appropriate meal planning, blood pressure and lipid management, and practical support for everyday eating.";s:3:"why";s:112:"We coordinate with neurology and therapy teams so nutrition supports your wider rehabilitation goals throughout.";}i:17;a:4:{s:8:"category";s:23:"Cardiovascular Diseases";s:5:"title";s:27:"Peripheral Vascular Disease";s:4:"text";s:235:"Reduced circulation to the legs causes pain, slow healing and steadily reduced mobility. We address the underlying vascular risk factors with targeted nutrition, weight management, activity guidance and dedicated wound healing support.";s:3:"why";s:115:"Improving circulation and healing capacity helps protect limb function, comfort and long term independent mobility.";}i:18;a:4:{s:8:"category";s:21:"Specialized Nutrition";s:5:"title";s:18:"Oncology Nutrition";s:4:"text";s:196:"Cancer and its treatment often affect appetite, weight, taste and physical strength. We provide nutrition support that preserves lean muscle, manages treatment side effects and helps you recovery.";s:3:"why";s:119:"Our plans adapt around chemotherapy, radiotherapy and surgery schedules to keep intake consistent throughout treatment.";}i:19;a:4:{s:8:"category";s:21:"Specialized Nutrition";s:5:"title";s:26:"Gastrointestinal Disorders";s:4:"text";s:219:"Digestive conditions can make eating unpredictable, restrictive and genuinely uncomfortable. We use structured, to identify triggers, correct nutrient deficiencies and rebuild a varied diet you can tolerate confidently.";s:3:"why";s:109:"We avoid unnecessary long term restriction and work steadily towards reintroducing foods wherever it is safe.";}i:20;a:4:{s:8:"category";s:21:"Specialized Nutrition";s:5:"title";s:24:"Stress-induced Gastritis";s:4:"text";s:220:"Stress, irregular eating and medication use can inflame the stomach lining and cause persistent discomfort. We combine meal timing, dietary modification and stress management to calm symptoms and support mucosal healing.";s:3:"why";s:92:"We treat the digestive symptoms and the daily habits, timings and stressors that drive them.";}i:21;a:4:{s:8:"category";s:21:"Specialized Nutrition";s:5:"title";s:23:"Liver Disease Nutrition";s:4:"text";s:214:"Liver disease alters how the body processes protein, salt, fluid and essential micronutrients. We design plans that maintain muscle mass, manage fluid retention and support liver function at every stage of illness.";s:3:"why";s:112:"Nutrition is adjusted as liver function changes, with regular clinical, biochemical and body composition review.";}i:22;a:4:{s:8:"category";s:21:"Specialized Nutrition";s:5:"title";s:35:"Endocrine Disorders (PCOS, Thyroid)";s:4:"text";s:230:"Hormonal conditions affect weight, energy, cycles, skin and mood in ways diet strongly influences. We provide targeted nutrition and lifestyle therapy that improves hormonal balance, metabolic markers and everyday symptom control.";s:3:"why";s:93:"We address the hormonal and metabolic drivers together, rather than focusing on weight alone.";}i:23;a:4:{s:8:"category";s:21:"Specialized Nutrition";s:5:"title";s:19:"Pediatric Nutrition";s:4:"text";s:214:"Children have changing nutritional needs that shape growth, immunity, learning and lifelong eating habits. We provide age appropriate assessment and family centred plans for growth concerns, and medical conditions.";s:3:"why";s:111:"Plans are practical for families, protecting healthy growth without creating pressure or conflict at mealtimes.";}i:24;a:4:{s:8:"category";s:37:"Geriatric & Palliative Care Nutrition";s:5:"title";s:34:"Frailty & Age-related Malnutrition";s:4:"text";s:213:"Reduced appetite, dental problems and illness often cause unintentional weight loss in older adults. We provide enriched, easy to eat nutrition plans that restore strength, energy, immunity and daily independence.";s:3:"why";s:114:"We screen for malnutrition early and use realistic, appealing food based solutions before considering supplements.";}i:25;a:4:{s:8:"category";s:37:"Geriatric & Palliative Care Nutrition";s:5:"title";s:8:"Cachexia";s:4:"text";s:220:"Cachexia causes severe muscle and weight loss that ordinary eating alone cannot reverse. We provide intensive nutritional and metabolic support to slow decline, preserve strength and maintain comfort and quality of life.";s:3:"why";s:109:"Our goals are set honestly and compassionately, focusing on comfort, function and realistic clinical benefit.";}i:26;a:4:{s:8:"category";s:37:"Geriatric & Palliative Care Nutrition";s:5:"title";s:31:"End-of-life Nutritional Support";s:4:"text";s:241:"In advanced illness, the purpose of nutrition shifts from treatment towards comfort and dignity. We provide gentle, individualised guidance that respects patient wishes and supports families through difficult and emotional feeding decisions.";s:3:"why";s:103:"We prioritise comfort, choice and dignity, supporting both the patient and the wider family throughout.";}i:27;a:4:{s:8:"category";s:37:"Geriatric & Palliative Care Nutrition";s:5:"title";s:20:"Dysphagia Management";s:4:"text";s:232:"Difficulty swallowing increases the risk of choking, chest infection and poor nutritional intake. We provide texture modified meal planning, safe feeding techniques and ongoing monitoring to protect both nutrition and airway safety.";s:3:"why";s:102:"Our plans follow recognised texture standards and are reviewed with speech and language therapy input.";}i:28;a:4:{s:8:"category";s:37:"Geriatric & Palliative Care Nutrition";s:5:"title";s:32:"Functional Decline & Muscle Loss";s:4:"text";s:222:"Loss of muscle strength reduces mobility, balance and confidence, raising the risk of falls. We combine higher protein nutrition, vitamin D support and resistance based activity to rebuild strength and functional capacity.";s:3:"why";s:112:"Progress is measured through practical strength, mobility and body composition changes rather than weight alone.";}i:29;a:4:{s:8:"category";s:32:"Aesthetic & Preventive Nutrition";s:5:"title";s:36:"Weight Management & Body Composition";s:4:"text";s:223:"Healthy change is about improving body composition, not simply lowering the number on the scale. We provide structured nutrition, activity and behavioural support that reduces fat mass while protecting valuable lean muscle.";s:3:"why";s:88:"We measure fat, muscle properly so your progress reflects real, lasting physical change.";}i:30;a:4:{s:8:"category";s:32:"Aesthetic & Preventive Nutrition";s:5:"title";s:34:"Skin Health & Anti-Aging Nutrition";s:4:"text";s:230:"Skin quality reflects hydration, blood sugar control, inflammation and overall micronutrient status. We provide targeted nutrition strategies that support collagen production, reduce inflammatory triggers and improve skin clarity.";s:3:"why";s:113:"We treat skin from the inside out, correcting internal deficiencies alongside your dermatology or aesthetic care.";}i:31;a:4:{s:8:"category";s:32:"Aesthetic & Preventive Nutrition";s:5:"title";s:33:"Hair Loss & Micronutrient Therapy";s:4:"text";s:218:"Hair thinning is frequently linked to iron, vitamin D, protein, thyroid or hormonal imbalance. We investigate the underlying cause and correct it with carefully tested, individualised micronutrient and dietary therapy.";s:3:"why";s:118:"Supplementation is guided by laboratory testing, never guesswork, and reviewed regularly for safety and effectiveness.";}i:32;a:4:{s:8:"category";s:32:"Aesthetic & Preventive Nutrition";s:5:"title";s:26:"Detox & Wellness Nutrition";s:4:"text";s:222:"Your body detoxifies naturally through the liver, kidneys and gut, given the right support. We provide evidence based programmes that improve digestion, energy, hydration and sleep, without extreme or restrictive cleanses.";s:3:"why";s:104:"We offer clinically sound wellness programmes rather than fad detoxes, crash plans or unproven products.";}i:33;a:4:{s:8:"category";s:32:"Aesthetic & Preventive Nutrition";s:5:"title";s:29:"Preventive Lifestyle Medicine";s:4:"text";s:219:"Most chronic disease is preventable when risk is identified and addressed early enough. We provide comprehensive screening and personalised nutrition, movement, sleep and stress plans that protect your long term health.";s:3:"why";s:99:"Prevention is built around your own risk profile, family history and current clinical test results.";}i:34;a:4:{s:8:"category";s:22:"Neurological Disorders";s:5:"title";s:21:"Stroke Rehabilitation";s:4:"text";s:223:"Neurological recovery is supported by consistent nutrition, safe swallowing and controlled vascular risk factors. We provide structured plans that support brain repair, restore strength and lower the risk of further stroke.";s:3:"why";s:111:"Nutrition therapy is coordinated with physiotherapy and speech therapy to support your full recovery programme.";}i:35;a:4:{s:8:"category";s:22:"Neurological Disorders";s:5:"title";s:38:"Dementia (e.g., Alzheimer’s Disease)";s:4:"text";s:230:"Dementia often affects appetite, mealtime routines, food recognition and the ability to eat independently. We provide practical nutrition strategies that maintain weight, hydration and dignity while supporting carers and families.";s:3:"why";s:116:"We provide realistic mealtime guidance for carers, reducing daily stress while improving overall nutritional intake.";}i:36;a:4:{s:8:"category";s:22:"Neurological Disorders";s:5:"title";s:21:"Parkinson’s Disease";s:4:"text";s:233:"Parkinson’s affects swallowing, digestion, medication timing and body weight in ways nutrition directly influences. We plan protein timing around levodopa, manage constipation and support stable weight, strength and safer mobility.";s:3:"why";s:109:"Meal timing is planned carefully around your medication schedule to help maintain consistent symptom control.";}i:37;a:4:{s:8:"category";s:22:"Neurological Disorders";s:5:"title";s:32:"Neuropathy (especially diabetic)";s:4:"text";s:221:"Nerve damage causes pain, numbness and reduced sensation, particularly in the feet and hands. We combine strict glucose control, targeted micronutrient therapy and foot care guidance to slow progression and ease symptoms.";s:3:"why";s:113:"Stabilising blood glucose remains the single most effective way to protect and preserve remaining nerve function.";}i:38;a:4:{s:8:"category";s:22:"Neurological Disorders";s:5:"title";s:36:"Epilepsy (Nutrition-sensitive cases)";s:4:"text";s:232:"Selected forms of epilepsy respond well to medically supervised ketogenic and modified dietary therapies. We assess suitability, initiate treatment safely and monitor closely to support seizure control and full nutritional adequacy.";s:3:"why";s:110:"Ketogenic therapy is delivered only under neurology supervision, with careful monitoring of growth and bloods.";}i:39;a:4:{s:8:"category";s:15:"Renal Disorders";s:5:"title";s:28:"Chronic Kidney Disease (CKD)";s:4:"text";s:236:"Kidney disease requires careful control of protein, sodium, potassium, phosphate and daily fluid intake. We provide stage specific plans that protect remaining kidney function, prevent malnutrition and delay progression toward dialysis.";s:3:"why";s:94:"Plans are adjusted at every stage of kidney disease, guided by your latest laboratory results.";}i:40;a:4:{s:8:"category";s:15:"Renal Disorders";s:5:"title";s:20:"Diabetic Nephropathy";s:4:"text";s:211:"When diabetes affects the kidneys, glucose and kidney focused nutrition must work carefully together. We balance blood sugar control with protein, management to protect kidney function and cardiovascular health.";s:3:"why";s:101:"We manage diabetes and kidney disease as one condition, avoiding plans that conflict with each other.";}i:41;a:4:{s:8:"category";s:15:"Renal Disorders";s:5:"title";s:46:"Dialysis Nutrition (Hemodialysis / Peritoneal)";s:4:"text";s:219:"Dialysis significantly changes daily protein, fluid, potassium and phosphate requirements. We provide tailored plans for haemodialysis and peritoneal dialysis that prevent malnutrition, control fluid gain and wellbeing.";s:3:"why";s:94:"Nutrition is matched to your dialysis modality, weekly schedule and most recent blood results.";}i:42;a:4:{s:8:"category";s:25:"Musculoskeletal Disorders";s:5:"title";s:14:"Osteoarthritis";s:4:"text";s:228:"Joint pain, stiffness and reduced movement are strongly influenced by body weight and inflammation. We combine weight management, anti-inflammatory nutrition and joint friendly activity to reduce pain and improve daily mobility.";s:3:"why";s:105:"Even modest weight reduction meaningfully lowers joint load, easing pain and improving everyday movement.";}i:43;a:4:{s:8:"category";s:25:"Musculoskeletal Disorders";s:5:"title";s:20:"Rheumatoid Arthritis";s:4:"text";s:250:"Autoimmune joint inflammation affects energy, appetite, bone health and long term physical function. We provide anti-inflammatory nutrition, bone protection and muscle preserving strategies that complement your prescribed rheumatology treatment plan.";s:3:"why";s:116:"Nutrition therapy supports your rheumatology treatment and helps manage medication related nutritional side effects.";}i:44;a:4:{s:8:"category";s:25:"Musculoskeletal Disorders";s:5:"title";s:10:"Sarcopenia";s:4:"text";s:216:"Age related muscle loss gradually reduces strength, balance, metabolism and personal independence. We combine higher protein intake, vitamin D correction and e training to rebuild muscle mass and functional strength.";s:3:"why";s:110:"Nutrition and resistance training are prescribed together, because muscle only rebuilds when both are present.";}i:45;a:4:{s:8:"category";s:25:"Musculoskeletal Disorders";s:5:"title";s:12:"Osteoporosis";s:4:"text";s:212:"Weakened bone increases fracture risk long before any symptoms or warning signs appear. We provide calcium, vitamin D, protein and weight bearing activity plans that protect bone density and reduce fracture risk.";s:3:"why";s:110:"Bone protection is planned alongside fall prevention, because both together determine your true fracture risk.";}i:46;a:4:{s:8:"category";s:25:"Musculoskeletal Disorders";s:5:"title";s:22:"Chronic Pain Syndromes";s:4:"text";s:225:"Persistent pain is influenced by inflammation, sleep quality, stress, activity levels and nutritional status. We provide an integrated plan addressing each of these factors to reduce pain intensity and restore daily function.";s:3:"why";s:101:"We address the whole picture, including sleep, stress and nutrition, rather than treating pain alone.";}}s:4:"more";a:2:{s:5:"title";s:23:"More ways GODC can help";s:5:"items";a:3:{i:0;a:4:{s:5:"title";s:18:"Lifestyle Medicine";s:4:"text";s:137:"Six evidence-based pillars of health: nutrition, physical activity, sleep, stress, social connection and avoidance of harmful substances.";s:4:"link";s:32:"/our-services/lifestyle-medicine";s:4:"icon";s:4:"leaf";}i:1;a:4:{s:5:"title";s:18:"Corporate Wellness";s:4:"text";s:127:"Evidence-based workplace wellness programs, seminars and health assessments for healthier employees and stronger organizations.";s:4:"link";s:32:"/our-services/corporate-wellness";s:4:"icon";s:8:"building";}i:2;a:4:{s:5:"title";s:24:"Global Health Consulting";s:4:"text";s:114:"Strengthening health systems and advancing sustainable development with governments, UN agencies, NGOs and donors.";s:4:"link";s:38:"/our-services/global-health-consulting";s:4:"icon";s:5:"globe";}}}s:3:"cta";a:5:{s:7:"eyebrow";s:24:"Not sure where to start?";s:5:"title";s:28:"Speak with our clinical team";s:4:"text";s:90:"Tell us about your health goals and we will guide you to the right service and specialist.";s:12:"button_label";s:19:"Book a Consultation";s:11:"button_link";s:20:"/book-a-consultation";}s:8:"featured";a:4:{s:5:"group";s:35:"Surgical, Bariatric & Diabetes Care";s:7:"eyebrow";s:24:"Prof. Dr. Mohsin Gillani";s:5:"title";s:35:"Surgical, bariatric & diabetes care";s:4:"text";s:93:"Obesity, diabetes and advanced laparoscopic surgery services led by Prof. Dr. Mohsin Gillani.";}}s:34:"015ee897037aa0e00a13bd009c5ad4b8sc";a:11:{s:5:"title";s:34:"Clinical & Critical Care Nutrition";s:7:"summary";s:98:"ICU, enteral and parenteral nutrition, post-surgical recovery and organ-failure nutrition support.";s:8:"metadata";a:2:{s:11:"description";s:165:"Clinical and critical care nutrition: ICU enteral and parenteral feeding, TPN, sepsis, trauma, post-surgical and organ-failure nutrition support by GODC specialists.";s:8:"keywords";s:107:"critical care nutrition, TPN, enteral feeding, ICU nutrition, post-surgical nutrition, parenteral nutrition";}s:4:"hero";a:2:{s:5:"title";s:34:"Clinical & Critical Care Nutrition";s:5:"intro";s:370:"Nutrition plays an essential role during critical illness, major surgery, trauma, and recovery. We provide specialized nutrition support for patients requiring advanced nutritional management, including enteral and parenteral nutrition when appropriate, while working collaboratively with the treating healthcare team to support recovery and optimize nutritional status.";}s:5:"signs";a:3:{s:5:"title";s:49:"Early Signs of Clinical & Critical Care Nutrition";s:4:"text";s:738:"Early signs that you may need clinical and critical care nutrition include unexplained weight loss, poor appetite, persistent fatigue, muscle weakness, and difficulty eating or swallowing. These symptoms may indicate that your body is not receiving the nutrients needed for recovery.

Individuals with serious illnesses, major surgeries, infections, or prolonged hospital stays may also experience increased nutritional needs. Without proper nutritional support, recovery can become slower and more challenging.

Recognizing these signs early allows healthcare professionals to provide timely nutritional intervention. A personalized nutrition plan can help improve strength, support healing, and reduce the risk of medical complications.";s:6:"images";a:1:{i:0;a:1:{s:5:"image";s:27:"clinical-critical-care.webp";}}}s:3:"cta";a:3:{s:5:"title";s:49:"Book a Consultation with our Nutrition Specialist";s:4:"text";s:351:"Our experienced nutrition specialists provide personalized clinical nutrition plans tailored to your medical condition and recovery needs. We work closely with your healthcare team to support healing, improve nutritional status, and promote faster recovery. Book your consultation today to receive expert nutritional care and long-term health support.";s:12:"button_label";s:19:"Book an Appointment";}s:6:"causes";a:3:{s:5:"title";s:49:"Why Is Clinical & Critical Care Nutrition Needed?";s:5:"intro";s:373:"Clinical and critical care nutrition is required when serious illnesses, injuries, or medical conditions increase the body’s nutritional needs. Patients who are unable to eat normally or have difficulty absorbing nutrients often need specialized nutritional support. Early nutritional intervention helps improve recovery, reduce complications, and support overall health.";s:5:"items";a:3:{i:0;a:2:{s:5:"title";s:33:"Critical Illness & Intensive Care";s:4:"text";s:213:"Patients in intensive care or with severe infections, trauma, or organ failure often have increased nutritional requirements. Specialized nutrition helps support healing, strengthen immunity, and promote recovery.";}i:1;a:2:{s:5:"title";s:22:"Major Surgery & Trauma";s:4:"text";s:210:"Following major surgery or serious injury, the body needs additional nutrients to repair tissues and regain strength. A personalized nutrition plan supports faster healing and reduces the risk of complications.";}i:2;a:2:{s:5:"title";s:26:"Chronic Medical Conditions";s:4:"text";s:238:"Long-term conditions such as cancer, kidney disease, liver disease, and gastrointestinal disorders can affect nutritional status. Clinical nutrition provides targeted dietary support to help manage symptoms and improve treatment outcomes.";}}}s:10:"conditions";a:4:{i:0;a:3:{s:5:"title";s:25:"Sepsis & Trauma Nutrition";s:4:"text";s:606:"Patients with sepsis or severe trauma may have increased nutritional needs during critical illness. Our nutrition support focuses on assessing nutritional status and providing an individualized plan based on the patient’s medical condition, energy needs, fluid requirements and ability to tolerate nutrition.

Depending on the clinical situation, nutrition may be provided through oral, enteral or parenteral routes. The plan is monitored and adjusted according to the patient’s condition and response to treatment, with the aim of supporting nutritional adequacy throughout critical care and recovery.";s:5:"image";s:13:"nutition1.jpg";}i:1;a:3:{s:5:"title";s:23:"Post-Surgical Nutrition";s:4:"text";s:616:"Nutrition plays an important role before and after major surgery, particularly when a patient is nutritionally at risk or unable to meet nutritional needs through normal food intake. We assess nutritional status and develop individualized nutrition support according to the type of surgery, medical condition and recovery needs.

When appropriate, nutritional support may include oral or enteral nutrition, with parenteral nutrition considered when adequate nutrition cannot be achieved through the digestive system. Nutrition is reviewed throughout recovery and adjusted according to the patient’s changing needs.";s:5:"image";s:16:"post-sugical.jpg";}i:2;a:3:{s:5:"title";s:31:"Organ Failure Nutrition Support";s:4:"text";s:653:"Patients with organ failure often require carefully planned nutrition because their energy, protein, fluid and electrolyte requirements can vary according to their condition and treatment. Our approach focuses on assessing the patient’s nutritional status and developing nutrition support that considers the affected organ and overall clinical condition.

Nutrition plans are monitored regularly to help maintain adequate nutritional intake while considering factors such as fluid balance, electrolytes and disease-specific requirements. Where needed, enteral or parenteral nutrition can be considered as part of a medically supervised nutrition plan.";s:5:"image";s:16:"organfailure.jpg";}i:3;a:3:{s:5:"title";s:32:"TPN (Total Parenteral Nutrition)";s:4:"text";s:612:"Total Parenteral Nutrition (TPN) provides nutrients directly into the bloodstream when a patient cannot receive adequate nutrition through the digestive system. It can provide nutrients such as carbohydrates, amino acids, fats, vitamins, minerals and electrolytes according to individual clinical requirements.

TPN requires careful clinical planning and monitoring, including nutritional requirements, fluid and electrolyte balance, venous access and potential complications. The nutrition plan is individualized and reviewed as the patient’s condition and ability to tolerate other forms of nutrition change.";s:5:"image";s:24:"Patient-starting-TPN.jpg";}}s:5:"risks";a:3:{s:5:"title";s:45:"Who Needs Clinical & Critical Care Nutrition?";s:5:"intro";s:412:"Clinical and critical care nutrition is essential for individuals with serious illnesses, complex medical conditions, or those recovering from major surgery or trauma. These patients often have increased nutritional requirements that cannot be met through a regular diet alone. Personalized nutritional support helps improve recovery, maintain strength, reduce complications, and enhance overall health outcomes.";s:5:"items";a:2:{i:0;a:3:{s:5:"title";s:16:"Critical Illness";s:4:"text";s:212:"Patients with severe infections, organ failure, or those admitted to intensive care often require specialized nutritional support. Proper nutrition helps strengthen the immune system and supports healing process.";s:3:"why";s:241:"GODC’s experienced nutrition specialists provide evidence-based nutritional care tailored to each patient’s medical condition. Our personalized approach supports recovery, improves nutritional status, and promotes better health outcomes.";}i:1;a:3:{s:5:"title";s:22:"Post-Surgical Recovery";s:4:"text";s:189:"Major surgery increases the body’s demand for nutrients needed for tissue repair and recovery. A personalized nutrition plan promotes faster healing and reduces the risk of complications.";s:3:"why";s:240:"At GODC, we work closely with patients and healthcare professionals to deliver individualized nutrition plans for every stage of treatment. Our focus is on enhancing recovery, preventing complications, and improving overall quality of life.";}}}s:9:"nav_group";s:27:"Clinical Nutrition Services";s:10:"card_image";s:27:"clinical-critical-care.webp";}s:34:"fff98bbdc135ae0f41985a5683cb53e7sc";a:7:{s:5:"title";s:18:"Lifestyle Medicine";s:7:"summary";s:85:"Six evidence-based pillars of health, delivered as a personalised clinical programme.";s:9:"nav_group";s:22:"Lifestyle & Programmes";s:8:"metadata";a:2:{s:11:"description";s:177:"Lifestyle Medicine at GODC: six evidence-based pillars — nutrition, physical activity, restorative sleep, stress management, social connection and avoiding harmful substances.";s:8:"keywords";s:138:"lifestyle medicine Lahore, six pillars of lifestyle medicine, preventive health, chronic disease reversal, lifestyle medicine consultation";}s:4:"hero";a:5:{s:7:"eyebrow";s:12:"Our Services";s:5:"title";s:18:"Lifestyle Medicine";s:4:"text";s:328:"Drawing on over 40 years of collective clinical and applied expertise, GODC’s multidisciplinary team translates lifestyle medicine from principle into measurable, lasting change improving health outcomes, enhancing quality of life, and sustaining long-term behavioural transformation across every dimension of how people live.";s:4:"form";s:13:"quick-booking";s:10:"form_title";s:19:"Book an Appointment";}s:7:"pillars";a:6:{i:0;a:7:{s:6:"anchor";s:9:"nutrition";s:7:"ordinal";s:10:"1st Pillar";s:5:"title";s:9:"Nutrition";s:4:"lead";s:32:"Fuelling the body with intention";s:4:"text";s:467:"Sustainable nutrition is not defined by restriction; it is built on daily choices that support energy, metabolic balance, and long-term immunity. Poor nutrition often manifests gradually through fatigue, weight fluctuation, hormonal imbalance, and escalating chronic disease risk.

GODC designs culturally relevant, evidence-based dietary strategies grounded in real behavioural patterns, producing consistent improvement that integrates naturally into everyday life.";s:4:"icon";s:5:"apple";s:5:"image";s:33:"Nutrition-Lifestyle-Medicine.webp";}i:1;a:7:{s:6:"anchor";s:16:"physicalactivity";s:7:"ordinal";s:10:"2nd Pillar";s:5:"title";s:17:"Physical Activity";s:4:"lead";s:35:"Keeping the body functionally alive";s:4:"text";s:399:"Movement is among the most powerful determinants of health, yet modern life systematically reduces it. Physical inactivity underpins cardiovascular disease, metabolic dysfunction, and declining functional capacity.

GODC develops individually tailored, structured movement plans that restore strength, mobility, and endurance through gradual, achievable progress without imposing unnecessary burden.";s:4:"icon";s:8:"activity";s:5:"image";s:41:"Physical-Activity-Lifestyle-Medicine.webp";}i:2;a:7:{s:6:"anchor";s:16:"restorativesleep";s:7:"ordinal";s:10:"3rd Pillar";s:5:"title";s:17:"Restorative Sleep";s:4:"lead";s:39:"The body’s biological recovery system";s:4:"text";s:389:"Sleep governs hormonal regulation, immune function, cognitive performance, and cellular repair. When disrupted, it affects nearly every physiological system often silently, well before symptoms become clinically apparent.

GODC identifies the root causes of sleep disruption and delivers structured, evidence-based interventions to restore healthy sleep architecture and circadian balance.";s:4:"icon";s:4:"moon";s:5:"image";s:41:"Restorative-Sleep-Lifestyle-Medicine.webp";}i:3;a:7:{s:6:"anchor";s:16:"stressmanagement";s:7:"ordinal";s:10:"4th Pillar";s:5:"title";s:17:"Stress Management";s:4:"lead";s:44:"Regulating the body’s response to pressure";s:4:"text";s:418:"Chronic stress is a significant and frequently underestimated driver of hypertension, metabolic disease, anxiety, and burnout. While stress is an inherent feature of high-performance life, its impact is determined by how effectively it is managed.

GODC equips individuals with practical coping frameworks, from behavioural modification to resilience-building techniques that integrate sustainably into daily routines.";s:4:"icon";s:5:"brain";s:5:"image";s:41:"Stress-Management-Lifestyle-Medicine.webp";}i:4;a:7:{s:6:"anchor";s:16:"socialconnection";s:7:"ordinal";s:10:"5th Pillar";s:5:"title";s:17:"Social Connection";s:4:"lead";s:38:"A biological requirement for wellbeing";s:4:"text";s:445:"Strong social relationships are directly linked to reduced disease risk, improved mental health, and increased longevity. Conversely, social isolation meaningfully elevates vulnerability to both physical and psychological illness.

GODC promotes structured approaches to strengthening social wellbeing within families, workplaces, and communities, recognising that health outcomes are profoundly shaped by the social environments people inhabit.";s:4:"icon";s:5:"users";s:5:"image";s:41:"Social-Connection-Lifestyle-Medicine.webp";}i:5;a:7:{s:6:"anchor";s:14:"substanceabuse";s:7:"ordinal";s:10:"6th Pillar";s:5:"title";s:31:"Avoidance of Harmful Substances";s:4:"lead";s:38:"Preventing long-term biological damage";s:4:"text";s:426:"Tobacco, excessive alcohol consumption, and other harmful substances remain among the most preventable causes of chronic disease and premature mortality, their effects accumulating silently until they become clinically significant.

GODC provides non-judgemental, clinically grounded support for risk reduction and cessation, combining rigorous assessment with practical behaviour change strategies tailored to the individual.";s:4:"icon";s:6:"shield";s:5:"image";s:29:"Drugs-Lifestyle-Medicine.webp";}}s:13:"summary_block";a:4:{s:5:"title";s:33:"Six Pillars of Lifestyle Medicine";s:4:"text";s:404:"These six pillars function as an interconnected system rather than isolated behaviours. Progress in one area reinforces gains across others; neglect in one can quietly undermine the whole. GODC’s approach is holistic, structured, and deeply personalized, designed to translate the science of lifestyle medicine into sustained improvements in functional health, quality of life, and long-term wellbeing.";s:12:"button_label";s:21:"Book Your Appointment";s:11:"button_link";s:20:"/book-a-consultation";}}s:34:"0fb97884fbf28c4681fe6bfd1bd65055sc";a:13:{s:5:"title";s:15:"Renal Disorders";s:7:"summary";s:74:"Kidney-safe nutrition for chronic kidney disease and diabetic nephropathy.";s:8:"metadata";a:2:{s:11:"description";s:168:"Renal nutrition for chronic kidney disease (CKD) and diabetic nephropathy. Protect kidney function with a personalised renal diet from GODC’s clinical nutrition team.";s:8:"keywords";s:88:"renal diet, CKD nutrition, diabetic nephropathy diet, kidney disease nutritionist Lahore";}s:4:"hero";a:2:{s:5:"title";s:15:"Renal Nutrition";s:5:"intro";s:363:"Kidney disease requires individualized nutrition management to help maintain overall health and reduce the risk of complications. We develop personalized nutrition plans for individuals with chronic kidney disease, nephrotic syndrome, and those receiving dialysis, considering laboratory results, stage of disease, medical treatment, and nutritional requirements.";}s:5:"signs";a:3:{s:5:"title";s:30:"Early Signs of Renal Disorders";s:4:"text";s:636:"Early signs of renal disorders can be subtle and may develop gradually over time. Common symptoms include fatigue, swelling in the feet or ankles, changes in urination, and persistent high blood pressure.

Some individuals may notice foamy or bloody urine, frequent urination at night, difficulty concentrating, or loss of appetite. These symptoms may indicate that the kidneys are not functioning properly.

Recognizing these warning signs early and seeking medical attention can help prevent further kidney damage. Timely diagnosis and appropriate treatment are essential for preserving kidney function and improving long-term health.";s:6:"images";a:2:{i:0;a:1:{s:5:"image";s:19:"renal-disorder.jpeg";}i:1;a:1:{s:5:"image";s:15:"disorders-.jpeg";}}}s:3:"cta";a:3:{s:5:"title";s:49:"Book a Consultation with our Nutrition Specialist";s:4:"text";s:351:"Proper nutrition plays a vital role in managing kidney health and supporting overall well-being. Our nutrition specialists create personalized meal plans tailored to your kidney condition, helping you manage symptoms, maintain healthy kidney function, and improve your quality of life. Book a consultation today to receive expert nutritional guidance.";s:12:"button_label";s:19:"Book an Appointment";}s:6:"causes";a:3:{s:5:"title";s:25:"Causes of Renal Disorders";s:5:"intro";s:333:"Renal disorders can develop due to a variety of medical conditions and lifestyle factors that damage the kidneys over time. Common causes include diabetes, high blood pressure, infections, kidney stones, and certain medications. Early identification of these causes can help prevent kidney damage and support long-term kidney health.";s:5:"items";a:3:{i:0;a:2:{s:5:"title";s:8:"Diabetes";s:4:"text";s:193:"Diabetes is one of the leading causes of kidney disease. High blood sugar levels can damage the small blood vessels in the kidneys over time, reducing their ability to filter waste effectively.";}i:1;a:2:{s:5:"title";s:19:"High Blood Pressure";s:4:"text";s:195:"Uncontrolled high blood pressure places extra strain on the kidneys and can gradually damage kidney tissues. Proper blood pressure management is essential for maintaining healthy kidney function.";}i:2;a:2:{s:5:"title";s:26:"Kidney Infections & Stones";s:4:"text";s:219:"Recurring kidney infections and kidney stones can block or damage the urinary tract, leading to inflammation and reduced kidney function. Early treatment helps prevent long-term complications and protects kidney health.";}}}s:10:"conditions";a:2:{i:0;a:3:{s:5:"title";s:28:"Chronic Kidney Disease (CKD)";s:4:"text";s:522:"Our nutrition care for Chronic Kidney Disease focuses on supporting kidney health while maintaining adequate nutrition and overall well-being. We create personalized nutrition plans based on kidney function, medical history, laboratory results, medications, and individual dietary needs.

Depending on the stage of CKD, we may provide guidance on protein, sodium, potassium, phosphorus, fluids, and overall dietary balance. Our goal is to support nutritional health and help manage factors that can affect kidney function.";s:5:"image";s:7:"ckd.jpg";}i:1;a:3:{s:5:"title";s:20:"Diabetic Nephropathy";s:4:"text";s:506:"Our nutrition approach for diabetic nephropathy focuses on supporting both kidney health and blood glucose management. Personalized plans consider diabetes control, kidney function, medications, laboratory results, weight, and individual lifestyle needs.

We provide guidance on balanced meals, appropriate carbohydrate and protein intake, sodium, and other nutrients according to kidney function. The goal is to support better metabolic health while helping protect kidney function and overall well-being.";s:5:"image";s:13:"diabetes.jpeg";}}s:5:"risks";a:3:{s:5:"title";s:50:"What increases the risk of Renal Disorders Health?";s:5:"intro";s:618:"If you have been diagnosed with a renal disorder, diabetes, high blood pressure, or are experiencing symptoms such as swelling, changes in urination, unexplained weight loss, or poor appetite, it is important to consult a nutrition specialist. Early nutritional support can help protect kidney function and manage your condition more effectively.

A nutrition specialist can develop a personalized meal plan based on your kidney health, medical condition, and nutritional needs. Proper dietary management can help reduce complications, improve energy levels, and support long-term kidney health and overall well-being.";s:5:"items";a:2:{i:0;a:3:{s:5:"title";s:24:"Kidney Disease Diagnosis";s:4:"text";s:212:"If you have been diagnosed with kidney disease or have abnormal kidney function tests, a nutrition specialist can help you manage your condition through a personalized kidney-friendly diet and lifestyle guidance.";s:3:"why";s:227:"GODC brings together experienced healthcare professionals who work collaboratively to provide comprehensive, patient-centered care. Our integrated approach ensures every patient receives the right treatment and ongoing support.";}i:1;a:3:{s:5:"title";s:34:"Persistent Kidney-Related Symptoms";s:4:"text";s:225:"Ongoing swelling, changes in urination, fatigue, poor appetite, or unexplained weight loss may indicate the need for nutritional support. Early consultation can help improve kidney health and reduce the risk of complications.";s:3:"why";s:228:"At GODC, every treatment plan is tailored to the individual’s unique health needs and goals. We focus on compassionate care, evidence-based practices, and long-term wellness to help patients achieve the best possible outcomes.";}}}s:4:"when";a:3:{s:5:"title";s:35:"When to see a Nutrition Specialist?";s:4:"text";s:291:"If you have chronic kidney disease, diabetes, high blood pressure, or have been advised to follow a special diet, consulting a nutrition specialist can help protect your kidney health. Early nutritional guidance can improve your overall well-being and slow the progression of kidney disease.";s:12:"button_label";s:19:"Book an Appointment";}s:9:"diagnosis";a:3:{s:5:"title";s:33:"How is Renal Disorders Diagnosed?";s:5:"intro";s:449:"Diagnosing renal disorders begins with a thorough review of your medical history, symptoms, and a physical examination. Your healthcare provider may recommend blood tests, urine tests, kidney function tests, imaging studies such as ultrasound or CT scans, and, in some cases, a kidney biopsy to determine the underlying cause. Early diagnosis helps preserve kidney function, guide effective treatment, and reduce the risk of long-term complications.";s:7:"columns";a:3:{i:0;a:3:{s:5:"title";s:6:"Causes";s:5:"intro";s:36:"Common contributing factors include:";s:5:"items";s:105:"Diabetes
High blood pressure
Kidney infections
Kidney stones
Autoimmune diseases
Long-term medication use";}i:1;a:3:{s:5:"title";s:9:"Treatment";s:5:"intro";s:72:"If symptoms are mild, your clinician may advise simple measures such as:";s:5:"items";s:119:"Prescription medications
Kidney-friendly diet
Blood pressure control
Dialysis
Lifestyle modifications
Kidney transplant";}i:2;a:3:{s:5:"title";s:15:"Predispositions";s:5:"intro";s:38:"You may be at higher risk if you have:";s:5:"items";s:79:"Family history
Advanced age
Advanced age
Diabetes
Diabetes
Chronic hypertension";}}}s:9:"nav_group";s:27:"Clinical Nutrition Services";s:10:"card_image";s:19:"renal-disorder.jpeg";}s:34:"9c72c120805dfa4014f3f413a7ddb790sc";a:9:{s:5:"title";s:13:"Medi Wellness";s:7:"summary";s:81:"Support for diabetic and obese patients, and for preventing diabetes and obesity.";s:9:"nav_group";s:35:"Surgical, Bariatric & Diabetes Care";s:6:"doctor";s:30:"/our-doctors/dr-mohsin-gillani";s:8:"metadata";a:2:{s:11:"description";s:156:"Medi Wellness in Lahore: health and taste food services, fitness and yoga, and beauty and body reshaping for diabetic and obese patients and for prevention.";s:8:"keywords";s:69:"medi wellness Lahore, diabetic diet, fitness and yoga, body reshaping";}s:4:"hero";a:4:{s:7:"eyebrow";s:24:"Prof. Dr. Mohsin Gillani";s:5:"title";s:13:"Medi Wellness";s:4:"lead";s:81:"Support for diabetic and obese patients, and for preventing diabetes and obesity.";s:5:"image";s:42:"The-Body-Camp-outdoor-yoga_Blog_Header.jpg";}s:7:"sidebar";b:1;s:3:"cta";a:4:{s:5:"title";s:49:"Book a consultation with Prof. Dr. Mohsin Gillani";s:4:"text";s:80:"Personalised obesity, diabetes and advanced laparoscopic surgery care in Lahore.";s:12:"button_label";s:19:"Book an Appointment";s:11:"button_link";s:20:"/book-a-consultation";}s:10:"card_image";s:42:"The-Body-Camp-outdoor-yoga_Blog_Header.jpg";}s:34:"d07816d13f1483a98bbcd99364e8440fsc";a:12:{s:5:"title";s:32:"Aesthetic & Preventive Nutrition";s:7:"summary";s:81:"Preventive and aesthetic nutrition for weight, skin, hair and long-term wellness.";s:8:"metadata";a:2:{s:11:"description";s:167:"Preventive and aesthetic nutrition: healthy weight management, skin and anti-aging nutrition, hair loss micronutrient therapy and detox wellness plans at GODC, Lahore.";s:8:"keywords";s:105:"aesthetic nutrition, anti-aging diet, hair loss nutrition, weight management Lahore, preventive nutrition";}s:4:"hero";a:2:{s:5:"title";s:32:"Aesthetic & Preventive Nutrition";s:5:"intro";s:353:"Healthy skin and energy levels often reflect overall health. We help identify nutritional and lifestyle factors that may contribute to concerns such as acne, pigmentation, premature skin aging, and persistent fatigue. Our evidence-based approach focuses on improving internal health to support healthier skin, increased vitality, and disease prevention.";}s:5:"signs";a:3:{s:5:"title";s:47:"Early Signs of Aesthetic & Preventive Nutrition";s:4:"text";s:788:"Early signs that you may benefit from aesthetic and preventive nutrition include low energy levels, unexplained weight changes, dull skin, hair thinning, brittle nails, or frequent digestive discomfort. These symptoms may indicate that your body is not receiving the nutrients it needs for optimal health.

Some individuals may also notice slow recovery after illness, weakened immunity, or difficulty maintaining a healthy weight despite their efforts. Poor dietary habits and nutritional deficiencies can affect both appearance and overall well-being.

Recognizing these signs early and seeking professional nutritional guidance can help prevent future health problems. A personalized nutrition plan supports healthy aging, enhances physical appearance, and promotes long-term wellness.";s:6:"images";a:1:{i:0;a:1:{s:5:"image";s:16:"nutrition-1.jpeg";}}}s:3:"cta";a:3:{s:5:"title";s:49:"Book a Consultation with our Nutrition Specialist";s:4:"text";s:332:"Achieve your health and wellness goals with personalized guidance from our experienced nutrition specialists. We create customized nutrition plans to support healthy weight management, radiant skin, improved energy, and disease prevention. Book your consultation today and take the first step toward a healthier, more confident you.";s:12:"button_label";s:19:"Book an Appointment";}s:6:"causes";a:3:{s:5:"title";s:50:"Why Is Aesthetic & Preventive Nutrition Important?";s:5:"intro";s:361:"Aesthetic and preventive nutrition plays a key role in maintaining overall health while enhancing physical appearance. A balanced diet provides the nutrients needed for healthy skin, hair, energy, and weight management while helping reduce the risk of chronic diseases. Personalized nutrition supports long-term wellness and encourages healthy lifestyle habits.";s:5:"items";a:3:{i:0;a:2:{s:5:"title";s:19:"Healthy Skin & Hair";s:4:"text";s:189:"Essential vitamins, minerals, and antioxidants nourish the skin and hair from within. A balanced diet helps improve skin texture, strengthen hair, and promote a healthy, natural appearance.";}i:1;a:2:{s:5:"title";s:17:"Weight Management";s:4:"text";s:210:"Personalized nutrition supports healthy weight management by providing the right balance of nutrients and calories. Maintaining a healthy weight reduces the risk of obesity and other lifestyle-related diseases.";}i:2;a:2:{s:5:"title";s:18:"Disease Prevention";s:4:"text";s:235:"Good nutrition helps strengthen the immune system and lowers the risk of chronic conditions such as diabetes, heart disease, and high blood pressure. Healthy eating habits promote long-term wellness and improve overall quality of life.";}}}s:10:"conditions";a:4:{i:0;a:3:{s:5:"title";s:36:"Weight Management & Body Composition";s:4:"text";s:485:"Our nutrition care for weight management focuses on achieving a healthy body composition through personalized nutrition and sustainable lifestyle changes. We consider your body composition, eating habits, activity level, health goals, and individual nutritional needs.

Rather than focusing only on the number on the scale, we aim to support healthy fat loss, muscle maintenance, energy, and overall well-being. Our plans are designed to help you achieve realistic and lasting results.";s:5:"image";s:11:"obesity.jpg";}i:1;a:3:{s:5:"title";s:34:"Skin Health & Anti-Aging Nutrition";s:4:"text";s:436:"Our nutrition approach for skin health focuses on providing the nutrients needed to support healthy skin and overall well-being. Personalized plans consider your dietary habits, lifestyle, nutritional needs, and individual skin-related goals.

We emphasize nutrient-rich foods, adequate protein, healthy fats, antioxidants, vitamins, minerals, and hydration. The goal is to support skin health from within while promoting healthy aging.";s:5:"image";s:14:"skin-aging.jpg";}i:2;a:3:{s:5:"title";s:33:"Hair Loss & Micronutrient Therapy";s:4:"text";s:519:"Our nutrition care for hair loss focuses on identifying and addressing potential nutritional gaps that may affect healthy hair growth. We assess dietary patterns and nutritional needs while considering factors such as protein, iron, zinc, vitamin D, and other essential nutrients.

Personalized nutrition guidance helps ensure adequate intake of key nutrients through a balanced diet and, when appropriate, targeted supplementation. Our goal is to support healthy hair growth while improving overall nutritional health.";s:5:"image";s:18:"hair-tretment.jpeg";}i:3;a:3:{s:5:"title";s:26:"Detox & Wellness Nutrition";s:4:"text";s:495:"Our wellness nutrition approach focuses on supporting healthy eating habits, hydration, digestion, energy, and overall well-being rather than relying on restrictive “detox” diets. We create practical nutrition plans based on your lifestyle, preferences, and health goals.

We emphasize whole foods, vegetables, fruits, fiber, adequate protein, healthy fats, and proper hydration. The goal is to support the body’s natural processes while building sustainable habits for long-term wellness.";s:5:"image";s:10:"detox.jpeg";}}s:5:"risks";a:3:{s:5:"title";s:54:"Who Can Benefit from Aesthetic & Preventive Nutrition?";s:5:"intro";s:571:"Aesthetic and preventive nutrition is beneficial for anyone looking to improve their overall health, maintain a healthy weight, and enhance their physical appearance through proper nutrition. It is especially valuable for individuals with poor dietary habits, nutritional deficiencies, or those aiming to prevent future health problems.

A personalized nutrition plan supports healthy skin, stronger hair, increased energy, better metabolism, and long-term wellness. Early nutritional guidance can help improve quality of life while reducing the risk of chronic diseases.";s:5:"items";a:2:{i:0;a:3:{s:5:"title";s:45:"Individuals Seeking Healthy Weight Management";s:4:"text";s:186:"People looking to lose weight, maintain a healthy body composition, or improve their metabolism can benefit from personalized nutrition plans that support sustainable, long-term results.";s:3:"why";s:230:"At GODC, we believe that good nutrition is the foundation of lifelong health. Our holistic approach combines personalized nutrition, lifestyle guidance, and preventive care to help you achieve lasting wellness from the inside out.";}i:1;a:3:{s:5:"title";s:44:"Individuals Focused on Wellness & Appearance";s:4:"text";s:182:"Those who want healthier skin, stronger hair, improved energy levels, and better overall well-being can benefit from targeted nutrition. A balanced diet helps enhance natural beauty.";s:3:"why";s:213:"Our nutrition specialists use evidence-based practices to create customized nutrition plans tailored to your health goals and individual needs. We focus on sustainable lifestyle changes that support better health.";}}}s:4:"when";a:3:{s:5:"title";s:35:"When to see a Nutrition Specialist?";s:4:"text";s:557:"If you are struggling with weight management, low energy, digestive issues, poor eating habits, or want to improve your overall health and appearance, it may be time to consult a nutrition specialist. Personalized nutrition guidance can help you achieve your wellness goals safely and effectively. A nutrition specialist can create a customized meal plan based on your lifestyle, health needs, and personal goals. Early nutritional support helps prevent future health problems while promoting long-term wellness, healthy aging, and improved quality of life.";s:12:"button_label";s:19:"Book an Appointment";}s:9:"nav_group";s:27:"Clinical Nutrition Services";s:10:"card_image";s:16:"nutrition-1.jpeg";}s:34:"5f17d8d0b66745f7fd34061e7a726bddsc";a:13:{s:5:"title";s:25:"Cardiometabolic Disorders";s:7:"summary";s:93:"Nutrition and lifestyle therapy for hypertension, type 1 and type 2 diabetes and prediabetes.";s:8:"metadata";a:2:{s:11:"description";s:163:"Specialist nutrition care for hypertension, type 1 diabetes, type 2 diabetes and prediabetes in Lahore. Evidence-based, personalised cardiometabolic plans at GODC.";s:8:"keywords";s:123:"diabetes diet Lahore, hypertension nutrition, prediabetes reversal, type 2 diabetes remission, cardiometabolic nutritionist";}s:4:"hero";a:2:{s:5:"title";s:25:"Cardiometabolic Disorders";s:5:"intro";s:401:"We provide nutrition care for individuals living with type 2 diabetes, prediabetes, insulin resistance, hypertension, coronary artery disease, metabolic syndrome, and related conditions. By evaluating your overall cardiometabolic health, we develop personalized lifestyle and nutrition plans that support healthy blood sugar levels, cardiovascular health, and sustainable long-term disease management.";}s:5:"signs";a:3:{s:5:"title";s:40:"Early Signs of Cardiometabolic Disorders";s:4:"text";s:834:"Persistent fatigue, low energy levels, and unexplained weight gain can be early indicators of cardiometabolic disorders. These symptoms often develop gradually and may be linked to changes in metabolism, insulin resistance, or underlying cardiovascular risk factors.

High blood pressure, elevated blood sugar levels, and abnormal cholesterol levels are common warning signs that should not be ignored. Regular health screenings can help identify these issues early, allowing for timely intervention and better long-term outcomes.

Excess abdominal fat, shortness of breath during routine activities, and reduced physical endurance may also signal cardiometabolic health concerns. Addressing these symptoms through lifestyle changes and medical care can help lower the risk of serious complications such as heart disease and diabetes.";s:6:"images";a:2:{i:0;a:1:{s:5:"image";s:19:"cardiometabolic.jpg";}i:1;a:1:{s:5:"image";s:26:"cardiovascular-disease.jpg";}}}s:3:"cta";a:3:{s:5:"title";s:49:"Book a Consultation with our Nutrition Specialist";s:4:"text";s:330:"Early evaluation and timely care can significantly improve long-term heart and metabolic health outcomes. Our certified specialists provide comprehensive cardiometabolic assessments and personalized treatment plans focused on improving cardiovascular function, optimizing metabolism, and supporting sustainable long-term wellness.";s:12:"button_label";s:19:"Book an Appointment";}s:6:"causes";a:3:{s:5:"title";s:35:"Causes of Cardiometabolic Disorders";s:5:"intro";s:395:"Cardiometabolic disorders develop due to a combination of lifestyle, genetic, and environmental factors that affect both heart and metabolic health. Poor dietary habits, lack of physical activity, obesity, and chronic stress can all contribute to insulin resistance, high blood pressure, and abnormal cholesterol levels, increasing the overall risk of cardiovascular and metabolic complications.";s:5:"items";a:3:{i:0;a:2:{s:5:"title";s:28:"Unhealthy Diet and Lifestyle";s:4:"text";s:209:"A diet high in processed foods, sugar, and unhealthy fats can lead to weight gain and metabolic imbalance. Combined with a sedentary lifestyle, it significantly increases the risk of cardiometabolic disorders.";}i:1;a:2:{s:5:"title";s:26:"Genetic and Family History";s:4:"text";s:185:"A family history of diabetes, hypertension, or heart disease can increase susceptibility. Genetic factors may influence how the body processes sugar, fat, and blood pressure regulation.";}i:2;a:2:{s:5:"title";s:29:"Chronic Stress and Poor Sleep";s:4:"text";s:183:"Long-term stress and inadequate sleep disrupt hormone balance and metabolism. These factors can contribute to weight gain, elevated blood pressure, and increased cardiometabolic risk.";}}}s:10:"conditions";a:4:{i:0;a:3:{s:5:"title";s:12:"Hypertension";s:4:"text";s:523:"Our nutrition care for hypertension focuses on supporting healthy blood pressure through personalized dietary and lifestyle strategies. We consider your eating habits, health history, activity level, and individual nutritional needs when creating your plan.

We emphasize balanced meals, appropriate portions, fruits and vegetables, whole grains, and healthier food choices while reducing excessive sodium and highly processed foods. The goal is to support better blood pressure control and long-term cardiovascular health.";s:5:"image";s:16:"hypertension.jpg";}i:1;a:3:{s:5:"title";s:24:"Type 1 Diabetes Mellitus";s:4:"text";s:494:"Our nutrition support for Type 1 Diabetes focuses on helping patients manage blood glucose while meeting their daily nutritional needs. Personalized meal planning takes into account insulin therapy, carbohydrate intake, activity levels, and individual lifestyle requirements.

We guide patients toward balanced meals, appropriate carbohydrate portions, and consistent eating patterns. Our goal is to support better glucose management, maintain energy, and promote overall health and well-being.";s:5:"image";s:9:"type1.jpg";}i:2;a:3:{s:5:"title";s:24:"Type 2 Diabetes Mellitus";s:4:"text";s:517:"Our nutrition care for Type 2 Diabetes focuses on improving blood glucose management through personalized meal planning and sustainable lifestyle changes. We consider your weight, eating habits, activity level, medications, and overall health when developing your nutrition plan.

We encourage balanced meals with appropriate portions, fiber-rich foods, quality protein, and healthier carbohydrate choices. These strategies can support better glucose control, healthy weight management, and improved metabolic health.";s:5:"image";s:10:"type-2.jpg";}i:3;a:3:{s:5:"title";s:11:"Prediabetes";s:4:"text";s:489:"Our nutrition approach for prediabetes focuses on improving blood sugar levels and reducing the risk of progressing to Type 2 Diabetes. We create practical meal plans based on your lifestyle, eating habits, weight, and individual health goals.

We focus on balanced meals, portion control, fiber-rich foods, and healthier carbohydrate choices while reducing excess sugar and highly processed foods. The aim is to support better metabolic health and encourage sustainable lifestyle changes.";s:5:"image";s:16:"pre-diabetes.jpg";}}s:5:"risks";a:3:{s:5:"title";s:53:"What increases the risk of Cardiometabolic Disorders?";s:5:"intro";s:400:"The risk of cardiometabolic disorders increases due to unhealthy lifestyle habits such as poor diet, physical inactivity, smoking, and excess body weight. Genetic predisposition, chronic stress, poor sleep, and existing conditions like diabetes or hypertension also raise the risk. When combined, these factors significantly increase the chances of developing long-term cardiometabolic complications.";s:5:"items";a:2:{i:0;a:3:{s:5:"title";s:22:"Lifestyle Risk Factors";s:4:"text";s:201:"Unhealthy eating habits, lack of exercise, smoking, and obesity significantly increase the risk of developing cardiometabolic disorders by affecting blood sugar, blood pressure, and cholesterol levels.";s:3:"why";s:185:"GODC builds a personalised, evidence-based nutrition plan around your diagnosis, medical history and goals, and tracks your progress against defined health markers throughout your care.";}i:1;a:3:{s:5:"title";s:25:"Medical & Genetic Factors";s:4:"text";s:179:"A family history of diabetes, heart disease, or hypertension, along with conditions like stress or poor sleep, can further raise the likelihood of cardiometabolic health problems.";s:3:"why";s:185:"GODC builds a personalised, evidence-based nutrition plan around your diagnosis, medical history and goals, and tracks your progress against defined health markers throughout your care.";}}}s:4:"when";a:3:{s:5:"title";s:35:"When to see a Nutrition Specialist?";s:4:"text";s:278:"You should see a cardiometabolic specialist if you experience symptoms such as persistent fatigue, high blood pressure, weight gain, or elevated blood sugar levels. Early evaluation can help identify underlying cardiometabolic disorders and prevent serious health complications.";s:12:"button_label";s:19:"Book an Appointment";}s:9:"diagnosis";a:3:{s:5:"title";s:43:"How is Cardiometabolic Disorders Diagnosed?";s:5:"intro";s:385:"Cardiometabolic disorders are diagnosed through a comprehensive evaluation that includes a review of your medical history, physical examination, and laboratory testing. Your healthcare provider may assess blood pressure, blood sugar levels, cholesterol levels, body weight, and other risk factors to determine your overall cardiometabolic health and identify any underlying conditions.";s:7:"columns";a:3:{i:0;a:3:{s:5:"title";s:6:"Causes";s:5:"intro";s:36:"Common contributing factors include:";s:5:"items";s:100:"Unhealthy diet
Physical inactivity
Obesity or excess weight
Smoking
Chronic stress
Poor sleep habits";}i:1;a:3:{s:5:"title";s:9:"Treatment";s:5:"intro";s:72:"If symptoms are mild, your clinician may advise simple measures such as:";s:5:"items";s:158:"Personalized nutrition plans
Regular physical activity
Weight management programs
Blood pressure control
Blood sugar management
Cholesterol-lowering therapies";}i:2;a:3:{s:5:"title";s:15:"Predispositions";s:5:"intro";s:38:"You may be at higher risk if you have:";s:5:"items";s:145:"Family history of heart disease
Family history of diabetes
Prediabetes or diabetes
High cholesterol levels
Metabolic syndrome
High blood pressure";}}}s:9:"nav_group";s:27:"Clinical Nutrition Services";s:10:"card_image";s:19:"cardiometabolic.jpg";}s:34:"3e95101d209f465731120010f4660554sc";a:9:{s:5:"title";s:13:"Diabetes Care";s:7:"summary";s:66:"Learn about diabetes and explore management and treatment options.";s:9:"nav_group";s:35:"Surgical, Bariatric & Diabetes Care";s:6:"doctor";s:30:"/our-doctors/dr-mohsin-gillani";s:8:"metadata";a:2:{s:11:"description";s:149:"Diabetes care in Lahore: understand the types of diabetes, how it is managed and treated, including metabolic surgery, with Prof. Dr. Mohsin Gillani.";s:8:"keywords";s:88:"diabetes treatment Lahore, metabolic surgery, diabetic foot care, Prof Dr Mohsin Gillani";}s:4:"hero";a:4:{s:7:"eyebrow";s:24:"Prof. Dr. Mohsin Gillani";s:5:"title";s:8:"Diabetes";s:4:"lead";s:66:"Learn about diabetes and explore management and treatment options.";s:5:"image";s:18:"New-Project-40.jpg";}s:7:"sidebar";b:1;s:3:"cta";a:4:{s:5:"title";s:49:"Book a consultation with Prof. Dr. Mohsin Gillani";s:4:"text";s:80:"Personalised obesity, diabetes and advanced laparoscopic surgery care in Lahore.";s:12:"button_label";s:19:"Book an Appointment";s:11:"button_link";s:20:"/book-a-consultation";}s:10:"card_image";s:18:"New-Project-40.jpg";}s:34:"bc55f82acea010ab0defa74fde3d0076sc";a:7:{s:5:"title";s:18:"Diabetes Treatment";s:7:"summary";s:58:"Advanced therapies for diabetic foot and neuropathic pain.";s:6:"doctor";s:30:"/our-doctors/dr-mohsin-gillani";s:8:"metadata";a:1:{s:11:"description";s:157:"Diabetes treatment in Lahore: diabetic foot care with hyperbaric oxygen, Dermapace and VAC dressing, plus neuropathic pain therapies such as Nerve Scrambler.";}s:4:"hero";a:3:{s:7:"eyebrow";s:24:"Prof. Dr. Mohsin Gillani";s:5:"title";s:18:"Diabetes Treatment";s:4:"lead";s:58:"Advanced therapies for diabetic foot and neuropathic pain.";}s:7:"sidebar";b:1;s:3:"cta";a:4:{s:5:"title";s:49:"Book a consultation with Prof. Dr. Mohsin Gillani";s:4:"text";s:80:"Personalised obesity, diabetes and advanced laparoscopic surgery care in Lahore.";s:12:"button_label";s:19:"Book an Appointment";s:11:"button_link";s:20:"/book-a-consultation";}}s:34:"b5a54b1e8d91c877c939bf2ce4e10772sc";a:7:{s:5:"title";s:35:"Type-2 Diabetes & Metabolic Surgery";s:7:"summary";s:104:"The role of metabolic surgery in type-2 diabetes mellitus, with its complications and treatment options.";s:6:"doctor";s:30:"/our-doctors/dr-mohsin-gillani";s:8:"metadata";a:1:{s:11:"description";s:152:"Type-2 diabetes in Lahore: causes, complications, why to treat it, and how bariatric/metabolic surgery can help. Guidance from Prof. Dr. Mohsin Gillani.";}s:4:"hero";a:3:{s:7:"eyebrow";s:24:"Prof. Dr. Mohsin Gillani";s:5:"title";s:15:"Type-2 Diabetes";s:4:"lead";s:104:"The role of metabolic surgery in type-2 diabetes mellitus, with its complications and treatment options.";}s:7:"sidebar";b:1;s:3:"cta";a:4:{s:5:"title";s:49:"Book a consultation with Prof. Dr. Mohsin Gillani";s:4:"text";s:80:"Personalised obesity, diabetes and advanced laparoscopic surgery care in Lahore.";s:12:"button_label";s:19:"Book an Appointment";s:11:"button_link";s:20:"/book-a-consultation";}}s:34:"1c812752fa0b3f8ffc4fdbf823cecb24sc";a:7:{s:5:"title";s:19:"Diabetes Management";s:7:"summary";s:100:"Surgical, medical and non-surgical approaches to managing diabetes and preventing its complications.";s:6:"doctor";s:30:"/our-doctors/dr-mohsin-gillani";s:8:"metadata";a:1:{s:11:"description";s:150:"Diabetes management in Lahore: surgical, medical and non-surgical options, treating complications with therapies and devices, and preventing diabetes.";}s:4:"hero";a:3:{s:7:"eyebrow";s:24:"Prof. Dr. Mohsin Gillani";s:5:"title";s:19:"Diabetes Management";s:4:"lead";s:100:"Surgical, medical and non-surgical approaches to managing diabetes and preventing its complications.";}s:7:"sidebar";b:1;s:3:"cta";a:4:{s:5:"title";s:49:"Book a consultation with Prof. Dr. Mohsin Gillani";s:4:"text";s:80:"Personalised obesity, diabetes and advanced laparoscopic surgery care in Lahore.";s:12:"button_label";s:19:"Book an Appointment";s:11:"button_link";s:20:"/book-a-consultation";}}s:34:"919166c146300adc0fd9b4399c2e470csc";a:7:{s:5:"title";s:14:"About Diabetes";s:7:"summary";s:91:"A group of metabolic diseases characterised by raised blood glucose levels (hyperglycemia).";s:6:"doctor";s:30:"/our-doctors/dr-mohsin-gillani";s:8:"metadata";a:1:{s:11:"description";s:149:"What is diabetes? Understand Type-1, Type-2, gestational diabetes and LADA, their causes, treatment and prevention. Prof. Dr. Mohsin Gillani, Lahore.";}s:4:"hero";a:3:{s:7:"eyebrow";s:24:"Prof. Dr. Mohsin Gillani";s:5:"title";s:14:"About Diabetes";s:4:"lead";s:91:"A group of metabolic diseases characterised by raised blood glucose levels (hyperglycemia).";}s:7:"sidebar";b:1;s:3:"cta";a:4:{s:5:"title";s:49:"Book a consultation with Prof. Dr. Mohsin Gillani";s:4:"text";s:80:"Personalised obesity, diabetes and advanced laparoscopic surgery care in Lahore.";s:12:"button_label";s:19:"Book an Appointment";s:11:"button_link";s:20:"/book-a-consultation";}}s:34:"554385b4b261a0f796e644ec547fd648sc";a:13:{s:5:"title";s:22:"Neurological Disorders";s:7:"summary";s:101:"Brain-supportive nutrition for stroke rehabilitation, dementia, Parkinson’s disease and neuropathy.";s:8:"metadata";a:2:{s:11:"description";s:168:"Neurological nutrition support for stroke rehabilitation, dementia, Parkinson’s disease and diabetic neuropathy. Personalised clinical nutrition care at GODC, Lahore.";s:8:"keywords";s:112:"neurological nutrition, dementia diet, Parkinson’s nutrition, stroke rehabilitation diet, neuropathy nutrition";}s:4:"hero";a:2:{s:5:"title";s:22:"Neurological Nutrition";s:5:"intro";s:365:"Neurological conditions such as stroke, Parkinson’s disease, Alzheimer’s disease, and epilepsy often affect nutritional status and overall health. Our nutrition care is designed to complement medical treatment by supporting adequate nutrition, managing swallowing-related concerns when appropriate, and promoting overall neurological health and quality of life.";}s:5:"signs";a:3:{s:5:"title";s:37:"Early Signs of Neurological Disorders";s:4:"text";s:932:"Early signs of neurological disorders can vary depending on the condition, but they often begin with subtle changes that are easy to overlook. Common symptoms include frequent headaches, dizziness, numbness or tingling in the hands and feet, muscle weakness, and difficulty maintaining balance. These signs may develop gradually or appear suddenly and should not be ignored if they persist.

Changes in memory, concentration, or thinking ability can also be early indicators of a neurological condition. Some individuals may experience confusion, difficulty finding words, blurred or double vision, hearing changes, or problems with coordination.

Seeking medical attention at the first sign of persistent neurological symptoms is important for early diagnosis and effective treatment. A healthcare professional may recommend neurological examinations, imaging tests, or other diagnostic procedures to identify the underlying cause.";s:6:"images";a:2:{i:0;a:1:{s:5:"image";s:18:"Neurological-.webp";}i:1;a:1:{s:5:"image";s:17:"neurological.webp";}}}s:3:"cta";a:3:{s:5:"title";s:49:"Book a Consultation with our Nutrition Specialist";s:4:"text";s:330:"Take the first step toward better neurological health with expert nutritional guidance. Our nutrition specialist provides personalized diet plans and practical recommendations to support brain function, overall wellness, and your long-term health goals. Schedule your consultation today and begin your journey to a healthier life.";s:12:"button_label";s:19:"Book an Appointment";}s:6:"causes";a:3:{s:5:"title";s:32:"Causes of Neurological Disorders";s:5:"intro";s:319:"Neurological disorders can develop due to a variety of factors that affect the brain, spinal cord, or nervous system. Some causes are inherited, while others result from injuries, infections, or lifestyle-related conditions. Understanding these causes can help with early prevention, diagnosis, and effective treatment.";s:5:"items";a:3:{i:0;a:2:{s:5:"title";s:15:"Genetic Factors";s:4:"text";s:357:"Some neurological disorders are passed down through family genes, increasing the risk of developing certain conditions. These inherited genetic changes can affect how the brain and nervous system function over time. Although genetic disorders cannot always be prevented, early screening and medical care can help manage symptoms and improve quality of life.";}i:1;a:2:{s:5:"title";s:21:"Brain Injury & Trauma";s:4:"text";s:359:"Traumatic injuries to the head or spinal cord can damage nerve cells and disrupt communication within the nervous system. Falls, road accidents, sports injuries, or severe blows to the head are common causes. Depending on the severity of the injury, individuals may experience long-term neurological symptoms that require ongoing treatment and rehabilitation.";}i:2;a:2:{s:5:"title";s:31:"Infections & Medical Conditions";s:4:"text";s:347:"Certain infections, autoimmune diseases, strokes, and chronic medical conditions can harm the brain and nervous system. Inflammation or reduced blood flow may interfere with normal nerve function, leading to neurological complications. Prompt diagnosis and appropriate treatment can reduce the risk of permanent damage and support better recovery.";}}}s:10:"conditions";a:4:{i:0;a:3:{s:5:"title";s:21:"Stroke Rehabilitation";s:4:"text";s:505:"Our nutrition care during stroke rehabilitation focuses on supporting recovery, strength, energy, and overall nutritional health. We create personalized plans based on the patient’s condition, activity level, appetite, swallowing ability, and individual nutritional needs.

We focus on adequate protein, calories, hydration, and nutrient-rich foods while considering any swallowing or feeding difficulties. The goal is to support rehabilitation, maintain strength, and promote better overall well-being.";s:5:"image";s:24:"stroke-rehabiliation.jpg";}i:1;a:3:{s:5:"title";s:8:"Dementia";s:4:"text";s:497:"Our nutrition approach for dementia focuses on maintaining adequate nutrition, hydration, and healthy body weight as eating patterns and appetite may change over time. We develop practical meal plans based on the patient’s preferences, abilities, medical needs, and stage of disease.

We encourage nutrient-dense, easy-to-eat meals and simple routines that can make eating more manageable. Our goal is to support nutritional status, energy, and quality of life for patients and their caregivers.";s:5:"image";s:13:"dementia.jpeg";}i:2;a:3:{s:5:"title";s:21:"Parkinson’s Disease";s:4:"text";s:481:"Our nutrition care for Parkinson’s Disease focuses on maintaining strength, energy, healthy weight, and adequate nutrient intake. Plans are personalized according to symptoms, appetite, activity level, swallowing concerns, and individual dietary needs.

We provide guidance on balanced meals, protein, fiber, hydration, and practical eating strategies. Where medication timing may affect nutrition, dietary recommendations can be coordinated with the patient’s healthcare plan.";s:5:"image";s:10:"ension.jpg";}i:3;a:3:{s:5:"title";s:32:"Neuropathy (Especially Diabetic)";s:4:"text";s:500:"Our nutrition approach for diabetic neuropathy focuses on supporting blood glucose management and overall metabolic health. Personalized nutrition plans are designed around the patient’s dietary habits, diabetes management, lifestyle, and nutritional requirements.

We emphasize balanced meals, appropriate carbohydrate portions, fiber-rich foods, quality protein, and essential nutrients. The goal is to support better metabolic health while promoting healthy eating habits and overall well-being.";s:5:"image";s:14:"nueropathy.jpg";}}s:5:"risks";a:3:{s:5:"title";s:56:"Factors That Increase the Risk of Neurological Disorders";s:5:"intro";s:476:"Several factors can increase the likelihood of developing neurological disorders, including genetics, aging, medical conditions, and lifestyle habits. While some risk factors cannot be changed, many can be managed through healthy choices and regular medical care.

Understanding these risks allows for earlier detection and better prevention. Maintaining overall health and seeking timely medical attention can help reduce the chances of developing neurological complications.";s:5:"items";a:2:{i:0;a:3:{s:5:"title";s:5:"Aging";s:4:"text";s:243:"At GODC, we combine expert medical care with personalized treatment plans to support your neurological health and overall well-being. Our patient-focused approach ensures accurate diagnosis, compassionate care, and long-term health management.";s:3:"why";s:185:"GODC builds a personalised, evidence-based nutrition plan around your diagnosis, medical history and goals, and tracks your progress against defined health markers throughout your care.";}i:1;a:3:{s:5:"title";s:19:"Unhealthy Lifestyle";s:4:"text";s:251:"GODC is dedicated to delivering trusted, patient-centered healthcare with a focus on quality, innovation, and compassionate support. Our experienced specialists use advanced diagnostic techniques and personalized treatment plans to help every patient.";s:3:"why";s:185:"GODC builds a personalised, evidence-based nutrition plan around your diagnosis, medical history and goals, and tracks your progress against defined health markers throughout your care.";}}}s:4:"when";a:3:{s:5:"title";s:35:"When to see a Nutrition Specialist?";s:4:"text";s:290:"If you experience persistent headaches, dizziness, numbness, memory problems, seizures, or difficulty with balance and coordination, it may be time to see a neurologist. Early evaluation can help identify the underlying cause and ensure timely treatment to protect your neurological health.";s:12:"button_label";s:19:"Book an Appointment";}s:9:"diagnosis";a:3:{s:5:"title";s:41:"How Are Neurological Disorders Diagnosed?";s:5:"intro";s:418:"Diagnosing neurological disorders begins with a detailed review of your medical history, symptoms, and a comprehensive neurological examination. Depending on the condition, your healthcare provider may recommend imaging studies, laboratory tests, or nerve function assessments to identify the underlying cause. An accurate diagnosis helps guide the most effective treatment plan and improves long-term health outcomes.";s:7:"columns";a:3:{i:0;a:3:{s:5:"title";s:6:"Causes";s:5:"intro";s:36:"Common contributing factors include:";s:5:"items";s:92:"Genetic conditions
Brain injuries
Infections
Stroke
Autoimmune diseases
Vitamin deficiencies";}i:1;a:3:{s:5:"title";s:9:"Treatment";s:5:"intro";s:72:"If symptoms are mild, your clinician may advise simple measures such as:";s:5:"items";s:86:"Prescription medications
Physical therapy
Occupational therapy
Lifestyle modifications";}i:2;a:3:{s:5:"title";s:15:"Predispositions";s:5:"intro";s:38:"You may be at higher risk if you have:";s:5:"items";s:64:"Family history
Advanced age
High blood pressure
Diabetes
Smoking";}}}s:9:"nav_group";s:27:"Clinical Nutrition Services";s:10:"card_image";s:18:"Neurological-.webp";}s:34:"640dc0b662602cf715e77769b96faf9csc";a:13:{s:5:"title";s:25:"Musculoskeletal Disorders";s:7:"summary";s:93:"Nutrition to protect bone, joint and muscle health in arthritis, sarcopenia and osteoporosis.";s:8:"metadata";a:2:{s:11:"description";s:172:"Nutrition therapy for osteoarthritis, rheumatoid arthritis, sarcopenia and osteoporosis. Protect bone, joint and muscle health with GODC’s clinical nutrition specialists.";s:8:"keywords";s:117:"osteoporosis diet, arthritis nutrition, sarcopenia treatment, musculoskeletal nutrition, bone health nutrition Lahore";}s:4:"hero";a:2:{s:5:"title";s:25:"Musculoskeletal Nutrition";s:5:"intro";s:328:"Nutrition is an important part of maintaining healthy bones, muscles, and joints. We provide individualized nutrition support for osteoporosis, sarcopenia, arthritis, injury recovery, and rehabilitation. Our goal is to promote bone health, preserve muscle mass, support physical function, and complement rehabilitation programs.";}s:5:"signs";a:3:{s:5:"title";s:40:"Early Signs of Musculoskeletal Disorders";s:4:"text";s:671:"Early signs of musculoskeletal disorders often begin with mild pain, stiffness, or discomfort in the muscles, joints, or bones. These symptoms may appear after physical activity or gradually worsen over time.

Some individuals may notice swelling, reduced flexibility, muscle weakness, or difficulty performing everyday movements such as walking, bending, or lifting. Joint tenderness and decreased range of motion are also common early indicators.

Recognizing these symptoms early and seeking medical evaluation can help prevent further damage. Timely diagnosis and appropriate treatment can improve mobility, relieve pain, and support long-term musculoskeletal health.";s:6:"images";a:1:{i:0;a:1:{s:5:"image";s:31:"musculoskeletal-disorders-1.jpg";}}}s:3:"cta";a:3:{s:5:"title";s:49:"Book a Consultation with our Nutrition Specialist";s:4:"text";s:382:"Take the first step toward better bone, joint, and muscle health with expert care from our musculoskeletal specialist. We provide comprehensive evaluations, personalized treatment plans, and rehabilitation strategies to reduce pain, restore mobility, and improve your overall quality of life. Book your consultation today and start your journey toward better musculoskeletal health.";s:12:"button_label";s:19:"Book an Appointment";}s:6:"causes";a:3:{s:5:"title";s:35:"Causes of Musculoskeletal Disorders";s:5:"intro";s:361:"Musculoskeletal disorders can develop due to a variety of factors that affect the bones, muscles, joints, ligaments, and tendons. Common causes include aging, repetitive movements, injuries, poor posture, and underlying medical conditions. Identifying these causes early can help prevent complications, reduce pain, and support long-term musculoskeletal health.";s:5:"items";a:3:{i:0;a:2:{s:5:"title";s:17:"Repetitive Strain";s:4:"text";s:190:"Repeated movements and overuse of muscles or joints can place excessive stress on the musculoskeletal system. Over time, this may lead to inflammation, pain, stiffness, and reduced mobility.";}i:1;a:2:{s:5:"title";s:15:"Injury & Trauma";s:4:"text";s:205:"Falls, sports injuries, accidents, or fractures can damage bones, muscles, ligaments, and tendons. Proper treatment and rehabilitation are essential to restore function and prevent long-term complications.";}i:2;a:2:{s:5:"title";s:20:"Aging & Degeneration";s:4:"text";s:210:"As the body ages, bones, joints, and muscles naturally lose strength and flexibility. This gradual wear and tear can increase the risk of conditions such as osteoarthritis, osteoporosis, and chronic joint pain.";}}}s:10:"conditions";a:4:{i:0;a:3:{s:5:"title";s:14:"Osteoarthritis";s:4:"text";s:486:"Our nutrition care for osteoarthritis focuses on supporting healthy body weight, joint health, and overall mobility through personalized dietary strategies. We consider your weight, lifestyle, activity level, eating habits, and individual nutritional needs.

We emphasize nutrient-rich foods, adequate protein, healthy fats, fiber, and a balanced diet while supporting healthy weight management. The goal is to promote overall joint and metabolic health and support an active lifestyle.";s:5:"image";s:8:"pain.jpg";}i:1;a:3:{s:5:"title";s:20:"Rheumatoid Arthritis";s:4:"text";s:480:"Our nutrition approach for rheumatoid arthritis focuses on supporting overall health and maintaining adequate nutrition alongside medical care. Personalized plans are developed according to your symptoms, lifestyle, medications, weight, and individual nutritional requirements.

We encourage a balanced diet rich in vegetables, fruits, whole grains, healthy fats, and quality protein. The goal is to support nutritional health, healthy body weight, energy, and overall well-being.";s:5:"image";s:14:"rhematoid.jpeg";}i:2;a:3:{s:5:"title";s:10:"Sarcopenia";s:4:"text";s:438:"Our nutrition care for sarcopenia focuses on maintaining and supporting muscle mass, strength, and physical function, particularly in older adults. We assess protein intake, body composition, activity levels, appetite, and overall nutritional status.

We focus on adequate protein, energy, and essential nutrients alongside appropriate physical activity. Our goal is to support muscle health, strength, mobility, and greater independence.";s:5:"image";s:14:"Sarcopenia.jpg";}i:3;a:3:{s:5:"title";s:12:"Osteoporosis";s:4:"text";s:467:"Our nutrition support for osteoporosis focuses on maintaining strong bones and providing the nutrients needed for healthy bone health. We create personalized plans based on age, dietary habits, medical history, lifestyle, and individual nutritional needs.

We emphasize adequate calcium, vitamin D, protein, and other nutrient-rich foods as part of a balanced diet. The goal is to support bone strength, healthy body composition, and long-term musculoskeletal health.";s:5:"image";s:13:"diabetes.jpeg";}}s:5:"risks";a:3:{s:5:"title";s:53:"What Increases the Risk of Musculoskeletal Disorders?";s:5:"intro";s:517:"Several factors can increase the risk of developing musculoskeletal disorders, including aging, obesity, repetitive physical activities, poor posture, lack of exercise, and previous injuries. Certain medical conditions, such as arthritis and osteoporosis, along with occupations that involve heavy lifting or prolonged sitting, can also place additional stress on the muscles, bones, and joints.

Understanding these risk factors and adopting healthy habits can help reduce the likelihood of musculoskeletal problems.";s:5:"items";a:2:{i:0;a:3:{s:5:"title";s:23:"Obesity & Excess Weight";s:4:"text";s:227:"Carrying excess body weight places additional stress on the bones, joints, and muscles, especially the knees, hips, and lower back. Maintaining a healthy weight can reduce strain and lower the risk of musculoskeletal disorders.";s:3:"why";s:171:"Our experienced specialists provide accurate diagnosis and personalized treatment plans to relieve pain, restore mobility, and improve your overall musculoskeletal health.";}i:1;a:3:{s:5:"title";s:34:"Poor Posture & Physical Inactivity";s:4:"text";s:227:"Poor posture and a sedentary lifestyle can weaken muscles, reduce flexibility, and increase pressure on the joints. Regular exercise and proper body mechanics help improve strength, mobility, and overall musculoskeletal health.";s:3:"why";s:162:"GODC offers advanced therapies and patient-focused rehabilitation programs designed to strengthen muscles, improve joint function, and support long-term recovery.";}}}s:4:"when";a:3:{s:5:"title";s:35:"When to see a Nutrition Specialist?";s:4:"text";s:361:"If you experience persistent joint pain, muscle weakness, back pain, stiffness, swelling, or difficulty moving, it is important to consult a musculoskeletal specialist. Early evaluation can help identify the underlying cause and prevent the condition from worsening. Timely treatment can relieve pain, restore mobility, and improve your overall quality of life.";s:12:"button_label";s:19:"Book an Appointment";}s:9:"diagnosis";a:3:{s:5:"title";s:43:"How is Musculoskeletal Disorders Diagnosed?";s:5:"intro";s:415:"Diagnosing musculoskeletal disorders begins with a detailed review of your medical history, symptoms, and a physical examination. Your healthcare provider may recommend imaging tests such as X-rays, MRI, CT scans, or ultrasound, along with blood tests if needed, to identify the underlying cause. An accurate diagnosis helps develop a personalized treatment plan, relieve symptoms, and restore mobility effectively.";s:7:"columns";a:3:{i:0;a:3:{s:5:"title";s:6:"Causes";s:5:"intro";s:36:"Common contributing factors include:";s:5:"items";s:75:"Repetitive strain
Sports injuries
Poor posture
Arthritis
Osteoporosis
Aging";}i:1;a:3:{s:5:"title";s:9:"Treatment";s:5:"intro";s:72:"If symptoms are mild, your clinician may advise simple measures such as:";s:5:"items";s:98:"Pain medications
Physical therapy
Lifestyle modifications
Joint injections
Rehabilitation programs";}i:2;a:3:{s:5:"title";s:15:"Predispositions";s:5:"intro";s:38:"You may be at higher risk if you have:";s:5:"items";s:73:"Advanced age
Obesity
Family history
Sedentary lifestyle
Previous injuries";}}}s:9:"nav_group";s:27:"Clinical Nutrition Services";s:10:"card_image";s:31:"musculoskeletal-disorders-1.jpg";}s:34:"75de040621cb19b09c92b71a3afa659dsc";a:11:{s:5:"title";s:18:"Corporate Wellness";s:7:"summary";s:94:"Evidence-based workplace wellness programs for healthier employees and stronger organizations.";s:9:"nav_group";s:17:"For Organisations";s:8:"metadata";a:2:{s:11:"description";s:166:"Corporate wellness programs by GODC: health seminars, employee health assessments, executive wellness and workplace campaigns built on Lifestyle Medicine in Pakistan.";s:8:"keywords";s:127:"corporate wellness Pakistan, employee health assessment, workplace wellness program, executive health, wellness seminars Lahore";}s:4:"hero";a:7:{s:7:"eyebrow";s:17:"For Organisations";s:5:"title";s:18:"Corporate Wellness";s:8:"subtitle";s:44:"Healthier Employees. Stronger Organizations.";s:4:"text";s:585:"At Gillani Obesity and Diabetes Clinic, we help organizations create healthier workplaces through evidence-based Lifestyle Medicine and corporate wellness programs. Our services are designed to support employee well-being, reduce health risks, and promote a culture of wellness that benefits both individuals and organizations.

Whether you are looking to introduce workplace wellness initiatives, provide health education, or offer personalized clinical support for your employees, we work with you to develop solutions that align with your organization’s goals and workforce needs.";s:12:"button_label";s:18:"Discuss Your Needs";s:11:"button_link";s:8:"#enquiry";s:5:"image";s:29:"Asian-Wellness-Corporate.webp";}s:8:"services";a:2:{s:5:"title";s:31:"Our Corporate Wellness Services";s:5:"items";a:5:{i:0;a:5:{s:5:"title";s:42:"Wellness Seminars and Educational Sessions";s:4:"text";s:230:"We deliver engaging, evidence-based seminars that empower employees to make informed lifestyle choices and improve their overall health. Sessions can be delivered in person or virtually and tailored to your organization’s needs.";s:10:"list_title";s:22:"Popular topics include";s:4:"list";s:210:"Workplace Well-being
Lifestyle Medicine
Healthy Nutrition
Weight Management
Physical Activity for Better Health
Stress Management
Sleep and Recovery
Diabetes Prevention and Management
Heart Health
Healthy Aging";s:5:"image";s:24:"Wellbeing-Corporate.webp";}i:1;a:5:{s:5:"title";s:27:"Corporate Wellness Packages";s:4:"text";s:140:"Every organization is unique. Our corporate wellness packages can be customized to meet the size, culture, and objectives of your workforce.";s:10:"list_title";s:24:"General packages include";s:4:"list";s:205:"Health education seminars
Lifestyle Medicine consultations
Nutrition consultations
Employee health risk assessments
Personalized wellness plans
Follow-up consultations
Wellness campaigns & awareness events";s:5:"image";s:13:"Employees.png";}i:2;a:2:{s:5:"title";s:40:"Executive Health and Leadership Wellness";s:4:"text";s:242:"Healthy leaders build healthy organizations. We offer personalized Lifestyle Medicine consultations and wellness support for executives and leadership teams, helping them manage health risks, improve resilience, and maintain peak performance.";}i:3;a:2:{s:5:"title";s:27:"Employee Health Assessments";s:4:"text";s:253:"Understanding employee health is the first step toward meaningful improvement. We offer individualized health assessments that help identify lifestyle-related risk factors and provide practical recommendations to support long-term health and well-being.";}i:4;a:2:{s:5:"title";s:28:"Workplace Wellness Campaigns";s:4:"text";s:274:"We partner with organizations to plan and deliver workplace wellness initiatives that encourage healthy behaviors and increase employee engagement. Campaigns can be designed around annual health observances or customized to address your organization’s specific priorities.";}}}s:3:"why";a:4:{s:7:"eyebrow";s:32:"Why Invest in Employee Wellness?";s:5:"title";s:38:"A healthy workforce benefits everyone.";s:5:"intro";s:54:"Corporate wellness initiatives can help organizations:";s:5:"items";s:223:"Promote healthier lifestyle habits
Support employee well-being
Improve workplace engagement
Encourage healthier workplace cultures
Increase awareness of preventable health conditions
Support long-term organizational success";}s:8:"approach";a:4:{s:7:"eyebrow";s:12:"Our Approach";s:5:"title";s:68:"Practical, engaging, and tailored to the needs of each organization.";s:5:"intro";s:135:"We believe successful wellness programs are practical, engaging, and tailored to the needs of each organization. Our approach includes:";s:5:"items";s:242:"Understanding your workforce and organizational goals
Developing customized wellness solutions
Delivering evidence-based education and clinical services
Encouraging sustainable healthy lifestyle habits
Supporting long-term employee well-being";}s:7:"clients";a:4:{s:7:"eyebrow";s:16:"Who We Work With";s:5:"title";s:39:"Designed for organizations of all sizes";s:5:"items";s:196:"Private companies
Corporate offices
Healthcare organizations
Educational institutions
Manufacturing and industrial organizations
Financial institutions
Technology companies
Nonprofit organizations";s:5:"image";s:29:"Asian-Wellness-Corporate.webp";}s:3:"cta";a:3:{s:7:"eyebrow";s:27:"Build a Healthier Workplace";s:5:"title";s:80:"Investing in employee well-being is an investment in your organization's future.";s:4:"text";s:166:"Whether you are planning a single wellness session or a comprehensive employee wellness program, GODC is ready to help you create a healthier, more engaged workforce.";}s:7:"enquiry";a:2:{s:5:"title";s:51:"Contact Us to Discuss Your Corporate Wellness Needs";s:4:"form";s:17:"corporate-enquiry";}}s:34:"3454773e1ca39e387949a9ed62621289sc";a:12:{s:5:"title";s:21:"Specialized Nutrition";s:7:"summary";s:106:"Condition-specific nutrition for oncology, gastrointestinal, liver and stress-related digestive disorders.";s:8:"metadata";a:2:{s:11:"description";s:170:"Specialized medical nutrition for oncology, IBD, IBS, malabsorption, gastritis and liver disease. Personalised, condition-specific plans from GODC clinical nutritionists.";s:8:"keywords";s:111:"oncology nutrition, IBS diet, IBD nutrition, liver disease diet, gastritis nutrition, medical nutrition therapy";}s:4:"hero";a:2:{s:5:"title";s:21:"Specialized Nutrition";s:5:"intro";s:443:"Some nutrition-related conditions require more than standard dietary advice. We provide comprehensive assessments and personalized nutrition interventions for individuals with severe malnutrition, rare metabolic disorders, unexplained nutritional deficiencies, and other complex clinical conditions. Our goal is to identify the underlying causes, develop targeted nutrition strategies, and monitor progress to support improved health outcomes.";}s:5:"signs";a:3:{s:5:"title";s:36:"Early Signs of Specialized Nutrition";s:4:"text";s:726:"Early signs that you may need specialized nutrition include unexplained weight loss, poor appetite, persistent fatigue, difficulty eating or swallowing, and frequent nutrient deficiencies. These symptoms can affect your body’s ability to heal and maintain overall health.

Some individuals may also experience digestive problems, muscle weakness, low energy levels, or difficulty managing chronic health conditions through diet alone. These changes may indicate that standard dietary advice is no longer enough.

Recognizing these signs early and consulting a nutrition specialist can help prevent complications. A personalized nutrition plan can improve nutritional status, support recovery, and enhance overall well-being.";s:6:"images";a:1:{i:0;a:1:{s:5:"image";s:24:"specialzed-nutrition.jpg";}}}s:3:"cta";a:3:{s:5:"title";s:49:"Book a Consultation with our Nutrition Specialist";s:4:"text";s:372:"Our experienced nutrition specialists provide personalized dietary guidance tailored to your unique health needs and medical conditions. We create evidence-based nutrition plans to support recovery, improve overall wellness, and help you achieve your long-term health goals. Book your consultation today to take the first step toward better nutrition and a healthier life.";s:12:"button_label";s:19:"Book an Appointment";}s:6:"causes";a:3:{s:5:"title";s:36:"Why Is Specialized Nutrition Needed?";s:5:"intro";s:395:"Specialized nutrition is needed when a person’s nutritional requirements change due to a medical condition, age, recovery, or specific health goals. Standard diets may not provide the nutrients required to support healing, manage symptoms, or maintain overall health. A personalized nutrition plan helps ensure the body receives the right nutrients for optimal recovery and long-term wellness.";s:5:"items";a:3:{i:0;a:2:{s:5:"title";s:26:"Chronic Medical Conditions";s:4:"text";s:217:"Diseases such as diabetes, kidney disease, heart disease, and cancer often require specialized dietary management. Personalized nutrition helps control symptoms, support treatment, and improve overall health outcomes.";}i:1;a:2:{s:5:"title";s:19:"Digestive Disorders";s:4:"text";s:189:"Conditions affecting the digestive system can reduce the body’s ability to absorb essential nutrients. Specialized nutrition plans help address deficiencies and support healthy digestion.";}i:2;a:2:{s:5:"title";s:18:"Surgery & Recovery";s:4:"text";s:209:"After surgery, injury, or serious illness, the body requires additional nutrients for healing and recovery. A tailored nutrition plan promotes tissue repair, strengthens immunity, and supports faster recovery.";}}}s:10:"conditions";a:4:{i:0;a:3:{s:5:"title";s:18:"Oncology Nutrition";s:4:"text";s:504:"Our oncology nutrition care focuses on maintaining strength, energy, and nutritional status throughout cancer treatment and recovery. We create personalized nutrition plans based on the patient’s condition, treatment, symptoms, appetite, and individual nutritional needs.

We focus on nutrient-dense foods, adequate protein, hydration, and practical meal strategies to help manage treatment-related challenges. Our goal is to support overall well-being and maintain nutritional health during treatment.";s:5:"image";s:12:"oncology.jpg";}i:1;a:3:{s:5:"title";s:52:"Gastrointestinal Disorders (IBD, IBS, Malabsorption)";s:4:"text";s:490:"Our nutrition care for gastrointestinal disorders focuses on managing digestive symptoms while ensuring adequate nutrition. Personalized plans are developed according to the condition, symptoms, food tolerance, nutritional requirements, and individual lifestyle.

We provide guidance on suitable foods, meal patterns, fiber, hydration, and nutrient intake to help support digestive health. The goal is to reduce discomfort, improve nutritional status, and develop sustainable eating habits.";s:5:"image";s:21:"gastrointestinal.webp";}i:2;a:3:{s:5:"title";s:24:"Stress-induced Gastritis";s:4:"text";s:476:"Our nutrition approach for stress-induced gastritis focuses on reducing digestive discomfort and supporting a healthier stomach environment. We develop personalized meal plans based on symptoms, eating patterns, food tolerance, and individual nutritional needs.

We encourage balanced, gentle meals and appropriate meal timing while identifying foods and habits that may worsen symptoms. The aim is to support digestive comfort and promote healthier long-term eating patterns.";s:5:"image";s:14:"gastritis.jpeg";}i:3;a:3:{s:5:"title";s:23:"Liver Disease Nutrition";s:4:"text";s:508:"Our liver disease nutrition care focuses on supporting liver function and maintaining adequate nutrition through personalized dietary strategies. Plans are tailored according to the type and stage of liver disease, nutritional status, lifestyle, and individual health requirements.

We focus on balanced nutrition, appropriate protein and energy intake, healthy food choices, and weight management where appropriate. Our goal is to support overall health and help patients maintain better nutritional status.";s:5:"image";s:18:"liver-patient.jpeg";}}s:5:"risks";a:3:{s:5:"title";s:32:"Who Needs Specialized Nutrition?";s:5:"intro";s:582:"Specialized nutrition is beneficial for individuals whose nutritional needs cannot be met through a regular diet alone. People with chronic diseases, digestive disorders, cancer, kidney disease, diabetes, or those recovering from surgery or serious illness often require personalized nutrition plans to support their health.

Proper nutritional care helps prevent deficiencies, manage symptoms, improve recovery, and enhance overall quality of life. A personalized approach ensures that each individual receives the right nutrients based on their medical condition and health goals.";s:5:"items";a:2:{i:0;a:3:{s:5:"title";s:33:"Individuals with Chronic Diseases";s:4:"text";s:224:"People living with conditions such as diabetes, heart disease, kidney disease, or cancer often have unique nutritional requirements. Specialized nutrition helps manage these conditions and supports better treatment outcomes.";s:3:"why";s:234:"GODC’s experienced nutrition specialists provide evidence-based dietary guidance tailored to your unique health needs. We focus on creating practical nutrition plans that support recovery, disease management, and long-term wellness.";}i:1;a:3:{s:5:"title";s:32:"Older Adults & Recovery Patients";s:4:"text";s:223:"Older adults and individuals recovering from surgery, injury, or prolonged illness may require additional nutritional support. Personalized meal plans help maintain strength, promote healing, and improve overall well-being.";s:3:"why";s:244:"Every patient is different, which is why GODC develops customized nutrition programs based on your medical condition, lifestyle, and health goals. Our patient-centered approach helps you achieve better outcomes and improve your quality of life.";}}}s:4:"when";a:3:{s:5:"title";s:35:"When to see a Nutrition Specialist?";s:4:"text";s:299:"If you are experiencing unexplained weight changes, poor appetite, digestive issues, or have a chronic medical condition, it is important to consult a nutrition specialist. Personalized nutrition guidance can help manage your condition, improve recovery, and support long-term health and well-being.";s:12:"button_label";s:19:"Book an Appointment";}s:9:"nav_group";s:27:"Clinical Nutrition Services";s:10:"card_image";s:24:"specialzed-nutrition.jpg";}s:34:"e209fa44d71fa6b56404ed9e429594basc";a:13:{s:5:"title";s:26:"Obesity & Metabolic Health";s:7:"summary";s:123:"Medically guided weight management and metabolic care for obesity, metabolic syndrome, insulin resistance and dyslipidemia.";s:8:"metadata";a:2:{s:11:"description";s:165:"Medically guided obesity and metabolic health nutrition in Lahore: personalised plans for weight management, metabolic syndrome, insulin resistance and dyslipidemia.";s:8:"keywords";s:133:"obesity treatment Lahore, metabolic syndrome diet, insulin resistance nutrition, dyslipidemia diet plan, weight management specialist";}s:4:"hero";a:2:{s:5:"title";s:38:"Weight Management and Metabolic Health";s:5:"intro";s:340:"Healthy weight management is about more than calorie restriction. We assess the biological, nutritional, and lifestyle factors that influence body weight and metabolic health to develop realistic, medically guided strategies that support sustainable weight management while improving overall health and reducing the risk of chronic disease.";}s:5:"signs";a:3:{s:5:"title";s:41:"Early Signs of Obesity & Metabolic Health";s:4:"text";s:956:"One of the earliest signs of obesity and metabolic health concerns is gradual weight gain, especially around the abdomen. Many individuals may notice increased fatigue, reduced stamina, or difficulty performing daily activities that were once easy. Changes in appetite, frequent cravings for sugary or high-calorie foods, and unexplained weight fluctuations can also indicate underlying metabolic imbalances.

Another common early warning sign is difficulty managing blood sugar levels. This may present as increased thirst, frequent urination, persistent hunger, or energy crashes throughout the day.

Physical signs may include elevated blood pressure, high cholesterol levels, or the development of darkened skin patches, particularly around the neck, underarms, or other skin folds. Shortness of breath during mild physical activity, joint discomfort, and increased waist circumference can also suggest the presence of obesity-related metabolic issues.";s:6:"images";a:1:{i:0;a:1:{s:5:"image";s:12:"obesity-.jpg";}}}s:3:"cta";a:3:{s:5:"title";s:49:"Book a Consultation with our Nutrition Specialist";s:4:"text";s:359:"Are you struggling with weight gain, low energy, or other signs of obesity and metabolic imbalance? Early intervention can make a big difference. Our certified obesity and nutrition specialists provide comprehensive evaluations and personalized nutrition plans designed to support healthy weight management, improve metabolism, and promote long-term wellness.";s:12:"button_label";s:19:"Book an Appointment";}s:6:"causes";a:3:{s:5:"title";s:36:"Causes of Obesity & Metabolic Health";s:5:"intro";s:318:"Obesity and metabolic health issues are caused by a combination of factors including poor dietary habits, lack of physical activity, and high intake of processed or high-calorie foods. Hormonal imbalances, genetic predisposition, stress, and inadequate sleep can also disrupt normal metabolism and lead to weight gain.";s:5:"items";a:3:{i:0;a:2:{s:5:"title";s:30:"Poor Diet and Lifestyle Habits";s:4:"text";s:284:"One of the main causes of obesity and metabolic health issues is an unhealthy diet and sedentary lifestyle. Frequent consumption of processed foods, sugary drinks, and high-calorie meals combined with low physical activity can lead to excess fat storage and slow metabolism over time.";}i:1;a:2:{s:5:"title";s:28:"Hormonal and Genetic Factors";s:4:"text";s:275:"Hormonal imbalances such as insulin resistance, thyroid disorders, or PCOS can significantly affect how the body processes and stores energy. In addition, genetics can play a role in determining how easily a person gains weight and how efficiently their metabolism functions.";}i:2;a:2:{s:5:"title";s:29:"Medical Conditions and Stress";s:4:"text";s:274:"Certain medical conditions and chronic stress can also contribute to obesity and metabolic dysfunction. Poor sleep, high stress levels, and conditions like diabetes or endocrine disorders can disrupt normal metabolic processes, making it harder to maintain a healthy weight.";}}}s:10:"conditions";a:4:{i:0;a:3:{s:5:"title";s:7:"Obesity";s:4:"text";s:498:"Our nutrition care for obesity focuses on personalized weight management plans designed around your body, lifestyle, eating habits, and health goals. We help you make realistic dietary changes without relying on extreme or restrictive diets.

Through balanced nutrition, portion guidance, and sustainable lifestyle strategies, we aim to support healthy weight loss, improve energy, and promote better overall health. Our approach focuses on building habits that can be maintained for the long term.";s:5:"image";s:11:"obesity.jpg";}i:1;a:3:{s:5:"title";s:18:"Metabolic Syndrome";s:4:"text";s:462:"Nutrition plays an important role in managing metabolic syndrome and its related risk factors, including excess weight, blood sugar, blood pressure, and cholesterol. We provide personalized meal plans based on your individual health needs and lifestyle.

Our approach focuses on balanced meals, better food choices, portion control, and improved eating patterns. These changes can help support metabolic health and reduce the risk of future health complications.";s:5:"image";s:21:"metbolic-syndrome.jpg";}i:2;a:3:{s:5:"title";s:18:"Insulin Resistance";s:4:"text";s:488:"Our nutrition care for insulin resistance focuses on improving blood sugar management through balanced meals and sustainable dietary habits. We consider your eating patterns, lifestyle, activity level, and individual health requirements when developing your plan.

We emphasize nutrient-rich foods, adequate protein, fiber, appropriate portions, and healthier carbohydrate choices. The goal is to support better insulin function, healthy weight management, and long-term metabolic health.";s:5:"image";s:12:"insuline.jpg";}i:3;a:3:{s:5:"title";s:12:"Dyslipidemia";s:4:"text";s:474:"Our nutrition services help manage unhealthy cholesterol and triglyceride levels through personalized dietary and lifestyle strategies. We assess your overall eating pattern and create practical recommendations that fit your health needs and daily routine.

We focus on increasing fiber-rich and nutrient-dense foods while encouraging healthier fats and balanced meals. These changes can support healthier lipid levels, weight management, and improved cardiovascular health.";s:5:"image";s:16:"dyslipidemia.jpg";}}s:5:"risks";a:3:{s:5:"title";s:54:"What increases the risk of Obesity & Metabolic Health?";s:5:"intro";s:414:"A diet high in processed foods, sugar, and unhealthy fats, combined with a sedentary lifestyle, significantly increases the risk of obesity and metabolic health problems. Lack of regular physical activity slows metabolism and leads to excess fat accumulation in the body over time.

In addition, lack of regular physical activity slows down metabolism and reduces the body’s ability to burn calories efficiently.";s:5:"items";a:2:{i:0;a:3:{s:5:"title";s:29:"Unhealthy Diet & Low Activity";s:4:"text";s:256:"Eating high-calorie junk food, sugary drinks, and oversized portions, along with little or no exercise, increases the risk of obesity. When the body burns fewer calories than it consumes, excess fat starts to build up, leading to metabolic health problems.";s:3:"why";s:185:"GODC builds a personalised, evidence-based nutrition plan around your diagnosis, medical history and goals, and tracks your progress against defined health markers throughout your care.";}i:1;a:3:{s:5:"title";s:29:"Genetics & Medical Conditions";s:4:"text";s:227:"Family history, hormonal imbalances (like thyroid issues or PCOS), and some medications can also raise the risk of obesity. These factors affect metabolism and make it easier for the body to gain weight even without overeating.";s:3:"why";s:185:"GODC builds a personalised, evidence-based nutrition plan around your diagnosis, medical history and goals, and tracks your progress against defined health markers throughout your care.";}}}s:4:"when";a:3:{s:5:"title";s:35:"When to see a Nutrition Specialist?";s:4:"text";s:275:"You should see a nutrition specialist if you are struggling with weight gain, obesity, or difficulty managing your eating habits despite trying on your own. They can help identify unhealthy dietary patterns and create a personalized plan for safe and sustainable weight loss.";s:12:"button_label";s:19:"Book an Appointment";}s:9:"diagnosis";a:3:{s:5:"title";s:44:"How is Obesity & Metabolic Health Diagnosed?";s:5:"intro";s:316:"Obesity and metabolic diseases are usually diagnosed through a combination of physical examination, medical history, and clinical measurements such as BMI, waist circumference, blood pressure, and blood tests. Doctors also assess lifestyle factors and related health conditions to confirm the diagnosis and severity.";s:7:"columns";a:3:{i:0;a:3:{s:5:"title";s:6:"Causes";s:5:"intro";s:36:"Common contributing factors include:";s:5:"items";s:101:"Unhealthy diet
Lack of exercise
Genetics
Hormonal imbalance
Stress and poor sleep
Certain medications";}i:1;a:3:{s:5:"title";s:9:"Treatment";s:5:"intro";s:72:"If symptoms are mild, your clinician may advise simple measures such as:";s:5:"items";s:98:"Regular physical activity
Weight loss plan
Better sleep habits
Stress management
Routine check-ups";}i:2;a:3:{s:5:"title";s:15:"Predispositions";s:5:"intro";s:38:"You may be at higher risk if you have:";s:5:"items";s:77:"Family history
Older age
Diabetes risk
High blood pressure
Hormonal disorders";}}}s:9:"nav_group";s:27:"Clinical Nutrition Services";s:10:"card_image";s:12:"obesity-.jpg";}s:34:"28de0c915e6253af9a2751d0b899c0d1sc";a:12:{s:5:"title";s:24:"Global Health Consulting";s:7:"summary";s:106:"Strengthening health systems and advancing sustainable development with governments, UN agencies and NGOs.";s:9:"nav_group";s:17:"For Organisations";s:8:"metadata";a:2:{s:11:"description";s:189:"Global Health Health Consulting: program design, health systems strengthening, MEAL, policy, workforce development and humanitarian program management for governments, UN agencies and NGOs.";s:8:"keywords";s:129:"global health consulting Pakistan, health systems strengthening, MEAL, humanitarian program management, public health consultancy";}s:4:"hero";a:7:{s:7:"eyebrow";s:13:"Global Health";s:5:"title";s:24:"Global Health Consulting";s:8:"subtitle";s:64:"Strengthening Health Systems. Advancing Sustainable Development.";s:4:"text";s:727:"At GODC, we partner with governments, healthcare organizations, development agencies, NGOs, UN organizations, corporations, and the private sector to strengthen health systems, improve program performance, and create sustainable impact. Our work goes beyond providing technical advice. We collaborate with organizations to solve complex challenges, transform ideas into measurable results, and build systems that continue to deliver value long after a project is completed.

Combining expertise in global health, public health, program management, policy development, governance, and workforce development, we help organizations make informed decisions, strengthen capacity, and improve outcomes for the communities they serve.";s:12:"button_label";s:25:"Discuss Your Requirements";s:11:"button_link";s:8:"#enquiry";s:5:"image";s:16:"Global-IHAM.webp";}s:8:"outcomes";a:3:{s:5:"title";s:34:"What We Help Organizations Achieve";s:5:"items";a:7:{i:0;a:2:{s:5:"title";s:17:"Stronger Programs";s:4:"text";s:340:"Successful programs begin with thoughtful planning and effective execution. We help organizations design, implement, and manage programs that are practical, evidence-based, and aligned with strategic priorities. From concept development to implementation and continuous improvement, we focus on delivering meaningful and measurable results.";}i:1;a:2:{s:5:"title";s:21:"Better Health Systems";s:4:"text";s:279:"Strong health systems improve access, quality, and equity of care. We work with organizations to strengthen health systems through strategic planning, policy development, service delivery improvement, and systems-level solutions that enhance long-term performance and resilience.";}i:2;a:2:{s:5:"title";s:33:"Evidence-Informed Decision Making";s:4:"text";s:278:"Better decisions are built on reliable evidence. We develop monitoring, evaluation, and learning frameworks that enable organizations to measure progress, assess impact, identify opportunities for improvement, and demonstrate accountability to stakeholders and funding partners.";}i:3;a:2:{s:5:"title";s:33:"Effective Policies and Governance";s:4:"text";s:289:"Clear policies and strong governance create the foundation for sustainable organizations. We support the development of policies, strategic frameworks, governance structures, and operational systems that improve accountability, strengthen leadership, and support effective decision-making.";}i:4;a:2:{s:5:"title";s:20:"Stronger Communities";s:4:"text";s:262:"Communities are at the heart of sustainable development. We help organizations design and implement community-centered initiatives that improve health, increase access to essential services, strengthen local capacity, and promote meaningful community engagement.";}i:5;a:2:{s:5:"title";s:33:"A Skilled and Resilient Workforce";s:4:"text";s:273:"People drive organizational success. We support workforce development through leadership development, technical capacity building, professional development, and organizational learning initiatives that strengthen individual performance and long-term institutional capacity.";}i:6;a:2:{s:5:"title";s:52:"Preparedness for Humanitarian and Emergency Response";s:4:"text";s:277:"Humanitarian settings demand coordinated, evidence-based action. We support organizations in strengthening preparedness, improving response planning, enhancing coordination, and implementing programs that protect vulnerable populations while supporting recovery and resilience.";}}s:3:"box";a:4:{s:5:"title";s:33:"Discuss your organization's needs";s:4:"text";s:165:"From preparedness through recovery, we help humanitarian organizations design programs that hold up when conditions don’t. Let’s talk about what your teams need.";s:12:"button_label";s:31:"Discuss Your Organization Needs";s:11:"button_link";s:8:"#enquiry";}}s:3:"how";a:5:{s:7:"eyebrow";s:11:"How We Work";s:5:"title";s:67:"Collaborative, practical, and tailored to each client's objectives.";s:5:"intro";s:81:"Every organization has unique priorities, challenges, and operating environments.";s:5:"items";s:275:"Understand organizational priorities and challenges
Identify opportunities for improvement
Design practical, evidence-based solutions
